// This Pine Script® code is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public License 2.0 at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/ MPL-2.0
//@version=6
// ============================================================================
//  MPC H4 SWEEP — liquidity sweep → candlestick confirmation → LTF close entry
// ============================================================================
// Aaron's own setup, written from his description on 2026-08-05. THREE timeframes,
// one job each:
//
//   LIQUIDITY (H4)     a new H4 opens; the PREVIOUS H4's high and low become the
//                      two levels. Price mitigating one of them starts a setup.
//                      High taken  → we want to SELL (fade the grab).
//                      Low taken   → we want to BUY.
//   CONFIRMATION (15m) the FIRST qualifying candlestick pattern to close AFTER the
//                      sweep, on the fade side. Its CLOSE becomes the trigger line
//                      (Aaron draws this by hand and labels it "15m.C.C").
//   ENTRY (chart, 5m)  the first chart candle to CLOSE beyond that line. That close
//                      IS the entry. Stop beyond the confirmation pattern's extreme.
//   EXIT               half off at 1:1, stop to breakeven on that same touch, and the
//                      rest rides a %-of-price ratchet with no target at all.
//
// ── WHY THERE IS NO 1:2 ANY MORE (Aaron, 2026-08-05) ─────────────────────────
// This file shipped with a fixed `rrRatio` of 2.0 and it is gone. The H4 sweep study
// (docs/H4_SWEEP_STUDY.md, Part 2) measured the SAME event set through both exits: a fixed
// 2R ceiling makes +0.117 expected R and a runner makes +0.409. The ceiling was throwing
// away two thirds of the edge, because a handful of trades that run a very long way carry
// the whole book — best single trade +25.4R, top five 71% of the profit. A+ Run 9 measured
// the identical shape on a different strategy (11 of 164 trades carried 106R of 109R), so
// this is the second independent time a fixed target has been the thing capping what pays.
// Raising 1:2 to 1:3 or 1:5 does not fix it; it moves the ceiling.
//
// ⚠ SO THE WIN RATE WILL FALL AND THAT IS NOT A REGRESSION. A runner gives back its open
// profit on the way out by construction, and the study's winning config wins 41% of the
// time. Read the expectancy and the drawdown, never the win rate — a 1:1-and-stop build
// wins far more often and makes less.
// ⚠ TP1 STILL EXISTS, and at 1:1, which is Aaron's own rule: half off at 1R takes the
// trade to a free ride and is what makes a 41% win rate survivable to hold through. It is
// also the one thing the study did NOT measure — every config there was all-or-nothing at
// the trail. So the 50% rung is a stated preference, not a measured optimum; sweep it.
//
// ⚠ THE CHART TIMEFRAME IS THE ENTRY TIMEFRAME. Run this on 5m. Pine reads HIGHER
// timeframes cleanly and lower ones badly (a 15m chart asking for 5m sees only the
// last 5m value inside the forming bar), so the entry has to be the chart itself and
// the other two are pulled up.
//
// ── SCOPE (Aaron, 2026-08-05) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ONE FILE. No export mirror, no cfg_ columns, no Python port, and nothing added to
// mpc_assistant.pine. This exists to answer one question — does the sequence produce
// trades, and are they worth anything — in the TradingView Strategy Tester. If it
// proves out, the port is a separate job with its own parity harness, and it will be
// a retrofit; that cost is known and accepted.
//
// ── WHAT IS NEW HERE, AND WHY IT HAD TO BE WRITTEN ───────────────────────────
// Nothing in this repo detects a Harami or an Engulfing. Not mpc_assistant.pine, not
// any engine, not any strategy. The labels on Aaron's chart come from a SEPARATE
// public indicator — "Candlestick Patterns Identified, update 1-17-26" by repo32 —
// and the fifteen definitions in the CANDLESTICK block below are ported from it
// VERBATIM, with exactly one deliberate change (see THE TREND FILTER IS GONE).
//
// Ported rather than re-derived on purpose. Aaron has been reading this setup off
// that indicator's labels for weeks; a Harami written from the textbook would mark
// different candles, and every disagreement would then read as a strategy result
// rather than a definition mismatch. That is this repo's most-repeated defect —
// two implementations of one idea, quietly disagreeing — and porting the source
// is the only thing that forecloses it.
//
// ── THE TREND FILTER IS GONE, AND IT IS THE ONE CHANGE FROM THE SOURCE ───────
// Every pattern in repo32's script ends with `open[trend] < open` (bearish) or
// `open[trend] > open` (bullish) — "was the open N bars ago below/above this one",
// N being a panel input defaulting to 5. It is a proxy for "price came up into this
// candle", and Aaron's call (2026-08-05) is that it is the wrong tool:
//
//   "Candlesticks should only be read at entry points for my setups, and if
//    liquidity has been swept."
//
// He is right, and the reason is worth keeping. The H4 sweep answers the same
// question PROPERLY — price did not merely rise, it took out a specific four-hour
// high and the stops resting behind it. A bars-ago price comparison is a weaker
// version of something the sequence already establishes. Worse, it was near-INERT
// here: you only look for a bearish pattern once the H4 high is swept, at which
// point price is at a high, so `open[5] < open` passes almost every time. It cost
// signals everywhere else and bought nothing here.
//
// ⚠ SO THIS STRATEGY WILL MARK CANDLES AARON'S OWN CHART DOES NOT. The filter only
// ever REMOVED patterns, so dropping it ADDS them back. That is intended, and it is
// why `showConfLabel` defaults ON — put this beside the indicator and the difference
// is visible candle by candle rather than inferred from a trade count.
//
// ⚠ THE LOCATION GATE REPLACES IT, AND IT IS DELIBERATELY NOT BAKED INTO DETECTION.
// Every pattern is detected on every 15m bar; the SWEEP decides which ones are read.
// Detection and permission stay separate for the same reason engines/news/ separates
// them ("the engine reports, the bot decides") and the FVG engine emits every gap
// with its direction flag and lets the consumer choose. Gate the detector instead and
// (a) this setup's gate stops serving the REV setup, which wants a fib band and a
// gap, not a sweep, and (b) the counterfactual is destroyed — you could never measure
// how many candles the location filter refused, which is the only way to learn
// whether it helps. The CANDLESTICK block below is self-contained for exactly this
// reason: wiring it into A+ later is copying one block and passing a different
// location, not untangling it from H4 logic it was written inside.
//
// ── WHAT CAME FROM THE "SWEEP AND ENGULF" SCRIPT, AND WHAT DID NOT ───────────
// Aaron brought a third-party script on 2026-08-05. Three of its ideas landed here and
// the rest was refused; recording both halves, because the refusals are the reusable part.
//
// TAKEN: (1) its signal, as the SWEEP + ENGULF pattern — one candle taking the previous
// candle's extreme and closing clean through the other side. It is genuinely stronger than
// repo32's Engulfing, which measures only against the previous candle's OPEN and ignores
// its wicks. (2) an ATR STOP as an alternative to the pattern extreme. (3) its
// previous-candle direction filter, generalised to name BOTH readings rather than only the
// one that script shipped.
//
// REFUSED, and why each would be a regression here:
//   · Its INVERT switch. Note it shipped defaulting to TRUE — the author is trading the
//     opposite of the thing the script is named after, which is a RESULT rather than a bug
//     and agrees with docs/H4_SWEEP_STUDY.md finding continuation dead and the fade real.
//     But with invert on, its EMA gates the PATTERN rather than the TRADE, so a short ends
//     up requiring price ABOVE the EMA. That is the exact defect `useEma`'s tooltip below
//     already names — it was written about this script.
//   · FIXED CONTRACT SIZING (`default_qty_value = 1`). Every trade then risks a different
//     amount, R stops meaning anything, and the curve is dominated by whichever trades
//     happened to carry the widest stops.
//   · Its DUPLICATE EXIT ENGINE — a hand-rolled `inTrade`/`hitTP`/`hitSL` state machine
//     running alongside `strategy.exit`, with the boxes drawn off the hand-rolled one, so
//     the picture and the Strategy Tester can disagree about the same trade.
//   · NO `process_orders_on_close`. It prices the stop and target off the close and then
//     fills at the next bar's OPEN, so its advertised 1:2 is measured against a price it
//     never filled at. See ORDER FILLS below.
//   · Its FIXED R:R, for the reason stated above.
//
// ── EIGHT OF THE FIFTEEN REPO32 PATTERNS CANNOT FIRE ON GOLD, AND THEY SHIP ANYWAY ──
// Gold's intraday opens equal the previous close except at the 18:00 NY reopen and
// the Sunday open. Substitute `open == close[1]` and eight patterns become
// arithmetically impossible:
//   Hanging Man    `high[1] < open`, but open == close[1] <= high[1]
//   Evening Star   `min(open[1],close[1]) > close[2]`, but open[1] == close[2]
//   Morning Star   the mirror
//   Shooting Star  `open > close[1]`
//   Piercing Line  `open < low[1]`, but open == close[1] >= low[1]
//   Bullish Belt   `open < lowest(10)[1]`, plus `low == open` exactly
//   Bull Kicker    `open >= open[1]` after a down candle
//   Bear Kicker    `open <= open[1]` after an up candle
// Every one needs a GAP. They are not deleted and not disabled in code — they get
// toggles like the rest, defaulted OFF, so the zero can be confirmed rather than
// taken on trust. A pattern that silently never fires is indistinguishable from a
// broken one, and this repo has been bitten by exactly that shape before.
//
// ⚠ HAMMER AND INVERTED HAMMER ARE USED BY SHAPE, NOT BY THEIR CLASSICAL NAME, and
// that will look like a bug if this note is not read. Both are classically bullish.
// Here the INVERTED HAMMER (long UPPER wick) is offered as a BEARISH confirmation and
// the HAMMER (long LOWER wick) as a bullish one. The reason is the location gate: an
// inverted hammer sitting on a freshly swept H4 high is a rejection of that high —
// it is the Shooting Star candle, which cannot fire here because it demands a gap.
// Neither carries a trend filter or a colour requirement in the source, so away from
// a location they are noise; the sweep is what makes them signal.
//
// ── ORDER FILLS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// `process_orders_on_close = true`. Aaron's rule is that the entry IS the close of
// the chart candle that closed beyond the line, and his own worked example prices it
// there (5m close 4255.97, stop 4264.35 — 8.38 of risk, so TP1 lands at 4247.59).
// Without this flag Pine fills a market order at the NEXT bar's open while
// the stop and target are still computed off the close, which is the defect in the
// script from the video Aaron took this idea from: an advertised 1:2 measured against
// a price the strategy never filled at. The honest way to price the real-world gap
// between "the close" and "your fill a second later" is Properties → Slippage, not a
// different fill model.
// ============================================================================
strategy("MPC H4 Sweep", overlay = true, initial_capital = 10000,
  default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1, pyramiding = 0,
  calc_on_every_tick = false, process_orders_on_close = true,
  max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 500)
//============================================================================
//  THE INPUT PANEL — one consolidated block, twelve numbered sections
//============================================================================
// Every strategy Pine in this repo uses the SAME numbered sections in the SAME order,
// so section 5 is Entry whichever file you open. A strategy with no fibs simply has no
// `9 · Drawing: fibs`; the numbering does NOT close up, because the number is the address.
//
// THE RULE THAT DECIDES A SECTION: ask what a setting CHANGES, never what it is ABOUT.
// It goes in 3-7 if it can move a trade, and 8-12 if it can only move a pixel.
//
// 🔴 THAT IS WHY THE FVG SETTINGS LIVE IN `5 · Entry` RATHER THAN AN "FVG" GROUP. Both
// min-gap floors, the middle-bar close test, the max-active cap and keep-until-broken all
// change WHICH GAPS EXIST, and therefore which entries fire — as does `eqExemptFvg`, which
// used to sit under Liquidity Levels. Grouping by NAME would have demoted five
// trade-deciding knobs to the bottom of the panel beside the fib colours, and nothing
// would have errored. A group named for an OBJECT attracts anything that mentions it;
// a group named for a JOB gives a new toggle exactly one honest home.
//
// ⚠ THIS BLOCK IS THE PANEL. Order here IS the order on screen: TradingView sorts groups
// by where each group's first input is declared and sorts within a group by declaration
// order. Do not scatter a new input back out to its use site — put it in its section here.
//
// ⚠ AN INPUT USED IN ANOTHER'S `active =` MUST BE DECLARED ABOVE IT. The section order
// already satisfies every such pair; keep it that way when adding one.
//
// ⚠ ADDING, REMOVING OR REORDERING AN INPUT RESETS SAVED CHART VALUES — TradingView keys
// them off declaration order within each type. `indicators/docs/PINE_INPUT_DEFAULTS.md` exists
// so that a pass like this can be PROVEN cosmetic by re-dumping and diffing rather than
// argued to be.
//============================================================================
var string G2 = "2 · Market structure"
var string G3 = "3 · What trades"
var string G4 = "4 · What arms it"
var string G5 = "5 · Entry"
var string G6 = "6 · Stop & targets"
var string G7 = "7 · Filters"
var string G8 = "8 · Chart annotations"

// ── 2 · Market structure ────────────────────────────────────────
// ⚠ THIS SECTION IS PURE DRAWING IN THIS FILE, AND THAT IS THE ONE THING TO KNOW ABOUT IT.
// Every other strategy here READS the structure engine — A+ prices its fibs off it, D's whole
// sequence is built out of SOS events. This one does not: it trades an H4 liquidity sweep
// confirmed by a candlestick pattern, and it consumes no swing, no BOS and no SOS. The engine
// was ported in on 2026-08-12 so that section 2 is identical on all five charts (Aaron: "on all
// of my strategies, the market structure should be the exact same"), and it can therefore never
// move a trade in this file — flip any of these four and the trade list is unchanged.
bool   showExternal     = input.bool(true,      "Show External Structure", group = G2, display = display.none)
bool   showInternal     = input.bool(false,     "Show Internal Structure", group = G2, display = display.none)
bool   showHistoricalInternal = input.bool(false, "Show Historic Internal Structure", group = G2, tooltip = "Keep internal structure labels and lines from previous swing ranges on the chart. Off = only show current swing range internals.", display = display.none)
bool   showSwingLabels  = input.bool(false, "Show Swing Point Labels", group = G2, tooltip = "Off = hide ASH/ASL, HH/HL, LH/LL and the internal swing point labels, leaving only BOS/SOS and iBOS/iSOS on the chart. The structure engine keeps running exactly as before — fibs, order blocks and the confirmation table are unaffected.", display = display.none)

// ── 3 · What trades ─────────────────────────────────────────────
bool execLongs  = input.bool(true, "Trade longs",  group = G3, tooltip = "On = long setups may trade. Off = shorts only. ⚠ A side switched off does NOT consume its H4 window here, unlike every other refusal in this file — so 'longs only' leaves the long book exactly as it is instead of quietly removing longs that shared a window with a short.")
bool execShorts = input.bool(true, "Trade shorts", group = G3, tooltip = "On = short setups may trade. Off = longs only. Refused triggers still carry their reason into the export as block code 5, so a disabled side is countable rather than invisible.")
string sizeMode = input.string("Risk % of equity", "Position sizing", options = ["Risk % of equity", "Fixed contracts"], group = G3, tooltip = "Risk % of equity = every trade risks the same FRACTION of the account, so every trade is exactly 1R and the results compound. Fixed contracts = the same quantity every time, whatever the stop distance, which is what most published scripts do. ⚠ Fixed is there to reproduce another script, not because it is better: with it, a trade with a $2 stop and one with a $20 stop count equally in the win rate but ten times apart in dollars, so profit factor and drawdown end up describing which trades happened to carry wide stops rather than whether the strategy works. Read R, not dollars, under Fixed.")
float riskPct   = input.float(1.0, "   ↳ Risk % per trade", minval = 0.01, maxval = 100, step = 0.1, group = G3, active = sizeMode == "Risk % of equity", tooltip = "Every trade risks this much of equity, so every trade is 1R and the R multiples on the chart mean the same thing across the whole run.")
float fixedQty  = input.float(1.0, "   ↳ Contracts", minval = 0.01, step = 0.01, group = G3, active = sizeMode == "Fixed contracts")
bool invertTrade = input.bool(false, "Invert (trade the opposite direction)", group = G3, tooltip = "ON = a bearish confirmation takes a LONG and a bullish one takes a SHORT. The stop moves to the other side of the same pattern, so risk stays measured on the candle that fired. ⚠ The script this came from ships this ON, which is the author saying the straightforward reading loses money. docs/H4_SWEEP_STUDY.md found the same thing on H4 sweeps: continuation is dead, the fade is real — and the fade is what this file already does with the switch OFF.")

// ── 4 · What arms it ────────────────────────────────────────────
string tfLiq  = input.timeframe("240", "Liquidity timeframe", group = G4, tooltip = "The timeframe whose PREVIOUS candle's high and low are the levels being swept. H4 by default. Its close is also the setup's clock: a new candle here rolls the levels and kills any setup that has not yet triggered.")
string tfConf = input.timeframe("15",  "Confirmation timeframe", group = G4, tooltip = "The timeframe the candlestick confirmation is read on. Its CLOSE becomes the trigger line. Must be lower than the liquidity timeframe and higher than the chart.")
bool reqSweep    = input.bool(true,  "Require an H4 sweep first", group = G4, tooltip = "ON = the sequence as designed: a liquidity level must be taken before any candlestick pattern is read, and the sweep decides the direction. OFF = patterns arm anywhere on the chart and supply their own direction, which is how an ordinary candlestick strategy works. ⚠ OFF also removes the one-setup-per-H4-window rule, because that window only exists to bound a sweep.")
bool confLive    = input.bool(false, "Read the confirmation bar as it closes (no 1-bar delay)", group = G4, tooltip = "OFF = the pattern is read from the last CLOSED confirmation bar, so the entry is one confirmation bar behind it. ON = the pattern is read on the bar it closes, with no delay. ⚠ ON is only equivalent when the confirmation timeframe EQUALS the chart timeframe — that is the case it exists for, and there it is exact and safe. On a HIGHER confirmation timeframe it reads a bar that is still forming, so the signal can appear and vanish inside the bar and the backtest will look better than anything you could have traded. Use ON only with the confirmation timeframe set to the chart.")
float dojiSize = input.float(0.05, "Doji size", minval = 0.01, step = 0.01, group = G4, tooltip = "repo32's own Doji tolerance: the body must be no more than this fraction of the candle's full range. 0.05 is his default.")
bool patBearSwpEng = input.bool(true,  "SELL · Sweep + Engulf",   group = G4, tooltip = "The strongest confirmation here, and the only one not from repo32. This candle takes out the PREVIOUS candle's HIGH and then CLOSES BELOW its LOW — a full outside-bar reversal. Strictly stronger than the Bearish Engulfing below, which only measures against the previous candle's OPEN and ignores its wicks entirely. Needs no gap, so it fires normally on gold. Ranked first, so a candle that is both is reported as this.")
bool patBearHarami = input.bool(true,  "SELL · Bearish Harami",   group = G4, tooltip = "Fires often. With no gap this reduces to: previous candle up, this one down, and it CLOSED ABOVE the previous candle's open. Momentum stalled without reversing.")
bool patBearEng    = input.bool(true,  "SELL · Bearish Engulfing", group = G4, tooltip = "Fires often. With no gap: previous candle up, this one down, and it CLOSED BELOW the previous candle's open. The exact complement of the Harami — together the two cover essentially every down-after-up candle, so running both is close to no pattern filter at all.")
bool patInvHammer  = input.bool(true,  "SELL · Inverted Hammer (upper wick)", group = G4, tooltip = "Long UPPER wick. Classically a bullish name, used here by SHAPE: on a freshly swept H4 high it is the rejection candle, i.e. the Shooting Star, which cannot fire on gold because it needs a gap. No trend or colour requirement in the source.")
bool patBearDoji   = input.bool(true,  "SELL · Doji",             group = G4, tooltip = "Indecision at a swept high. Carries no direction of its own — the sweep supplies it.")
bool patHangingMan = input.bool(false, "SELL · Hanging Man (needs a gap)",   group = G4, tooltip = "Requires `high[1] < open` — the open ABOVE the previous candle's high. Impossible on gold except at the 18:00 reopen or the Sunday open. On by all means, but expect nothing.")
bool patEveningStar= input.bool(false, "SELL · Evening Star (needs a gap)",  group = G4, tooltip = "Requires the middle candle's whole body to sit above the first candle's close — a gap up. Near-dead on a continuous instrument.")
bool patShootStar  = input.bool(false, "SELL · Shooting Star (needs a gap)", group = G4, tooltip = "Requires `open > close[1]`, a gap up. Use the Inverted Hammer instead — same candle, no gap demanded.")
bool patBearKick   = input.bool(false, "SELL · Bearish Kicker (needs a gap)",group = G4, tooltip = "Requires the open at or below the PREVIOUS candle's open after an up candle — a gap down. Near-dead here.")
bool patBullSwpEng = input.bool(true,  "BUY · Sweep + Engulf",    group = G4, tooltip = "Mirror of the bearish one: this candle takes out the PREVIOUS candle's LOW and CLOSES ABOVE its HIGH. A full outside-bar reversal, stronger than the Bullish Engulfing below and needing no gap. Ranked first.")
bool patBullHarami = input.bool(true,  "BUY · Bullish Harami",    group = G4, tooltip = "Mirror of the bearish Harami: previous candle down, this one up, closed BELOW the previous open.")
bool patBullEng    = input.bool(true,  "BUY · Bullish Engulfing", group = G4, tooltip = "Mirror of the bearish Engulfing: closed ABOVE the previous open, bigger body.")
bool patHammer     = input.bool(true,  "BUY · Hammer (lower wick)", group = G4, tooltip = "Long LOWER wick. Used by shape: on a freshly swept H4 low it is the rejection candle. No trend or colour requirement in the source.")
bool patBullDoji   = input.bool(true,  "BUY · Doji",              group = G4, tooltip = "Indecision at a swept low.")
bool patMornStar   = input.bool(false, "BUY · Morning Star (needs a gap)",   group = G4, tooltip = "Mirror of the Evening Star. Needs a gap down. Near-dead here.")
bool patPiercing   = input.bool(false, "BUY · Piercing Line (needs a gap)",  group = G4, tooltip = "Requires `open < low[1]` — the open BELOW the previous candle's low. Impossible without a gap.")
bool patBullBelt   = input.bool(false, "BUY · Bullish Belt (needs a gap)",   group = G4, tooltip = "Requires the open below the lowest low of the previous ten candles AND the low to equal the open exactly. Effectively unreachable here.")
bool patBullKick   = input.bool(false, "BUY · Bullish Kicker (needs a gap)", group = G4, tooltip = "Requires the open at or above the PREVIOUS candle's open after a down candle — a gap up. Near-dead here.")

// ── 5 · Entry ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool entryAtConf = input.bool(false, "Enter on the confirmation close (skip the trigger line)", group = G5, tooltip = "OFF = the confirmation candle's close becomes a LINE, and the entry waits for a chart candle to close beyond it. ON = enter as soon as the pattern confirms, with no second step. ⚠ ON is earlier and cheaper but takes every pattern; OFF is the rule as Aaron trades it and refuses a pattern the market never followed through on. ⚠ Even ON, the entry is one confirmation bar behind the pattern — this file reads the last CLOSED bar so nothing repaints, and that lag cannot be removed.")

// ── 6 · Stop & targets ──────────────────────────────────────────
string slMode   = input.string("Pattern extreme", "Stop placement", options = ["Pattern extreme", "ATR"], group = G6, tooltip = "Pattern extreme = the stop sits on the confirmation candle's high (short) or low (long), which is the rule as Aaron states it. ATR = a fixed multiple of the confirmation timeframe's ATR from the entry, ignoring the pattern's own size. Why ATR is worth testing: with the pattern extreme, a BIG confirmation candle gives you a wide stop AND — because TP1 is a multiple of it — a distant first target, so the same nominal 1:1 is materially harder to reach. ATR decouples the two. ⚠ It also decouples the stop from the thing that would invalidate the setup, which is the real argument for keeping the pattern extreme. Measure, do not assume.")
int    atrLen   = input.int(14, "   ↳ ATR length", minval = 1, group = G6, active = slMode == "ATR")
float  slMult   = input.float(1.5, "   ↳ ATR multiplier", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = G6, active = slMode == "ATR", tooltip = "Stop distance = this many ATRs from the entry. ⚠ The ATR is measured on the CONFIRMATION timeframe, not the chart — it is standing in for the size of the 15m pattern, so a 5m ATR would be the wrong scale by a factor of three and would produce stops far tighter than the candle it replaces.")
float stopBufTk = input.float(0.0, "Stop buffer beyond the pattern (ticks)", minval = 0, group = G6, active = slMode == "Pattern extreme", tooltip = "Extra room past the confirmation pattern's extreme, so a wick through it does not clip you. 0 = the stop sits exactly on the pattern's high (short) or low (long), which is the rule as stated.")
float tp1R      = input.float(1.0, "TP1 distance (R)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = G6, tooltip = "Where the first target sits, as a multiple of the stop distance. 1.0 = a 1:1 scale-out. This price does TWO jobs — it banks the TP1 rung, and touching it is what lifts the stop to breakeven. Both happen on the same touch, deliberately: keying breakeven off the TP1 TOUCH rather than off an R distance guarantees the partial is banked before the rest of the position is protected. The A+ file measured every decoupled R trigger (0.25 / 0.5 / 1R) as worse and its comment says not to separate them again.")
float tp1Pct    = input.float(50,  "TP1 size %", minval = 0, maxval = 100, step = 5, group = G6, tooltip = "How much of the position the TP1 limit banks. 50 = half off at 1:1, the rest rides the trail. 0 = bank nothing there, ride the whole position (the TP1 price still moves the stop to breakeven). ⚠ A rung sized 0 is SKIPPED, never placed — strategy.exit() reads qty_percent = 0 as 'unspecified' and closes the WHOLE position at that limit, which is the exact opposite of banking nothing.")
float beBufTk   = input.float(0.0, "Breakeven buffer (ticks)", minval = 0, group = G6, tooltip = "The breakeven stop sits this far past the entry, so a scratch still covers costs rather than closing at exactly zero. 0 = flat breakeven. Note that a non-zero buffer files the scratch as a small WINNER in the Strategy Tester; the R label on the chart counts it honestly.")
float trailPct  = input.float(1.0, "Runner ratchet step (% of price)", minval = 0.05, step = 0.05, group = G6, tooltip = "TP2 is not a price — it is this trail. Once TP1 is touched the stop sits at breakeven and then climbs one step of this size for every step of favourable move, so the runner has no ceiling. 1.0% is the A+ default, and on gold at $4,200 that is a ~$42 step against a stop of roughly $8, i.e. the ratchet only engages about 5R out and then moves in 5R chunks. That is a LOOSE trail by design — a runner needs room — but it is the first thing to sweep if the runners keep giving back their gains. ⚠ The A+ version anchors this ratchet on the last confirmed swing; there is no structure engine in this file, so it anchors on breakeven instead.")

// ── 7 · Filters ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
string prevDir = input.string("Any", "Candle before the confirmation", options = ["Any", "Ran into the level", "Already turning"], group = G7, tooltip = "What the confirmation candle's own PREDECESSOR had to be doing, read on the confirmation timeframe. Any = no filter. 'Ran into the level' wants that candle pushing TOWARD the swept level — price rose into the H4 high and was then rejected, which is the fade you are trying to take. 'Already turning' wants it moving the other way, i.e. the reversal was underway before the confirmation printed; this is the version the source script shipped, and it is the weaker read here because it fires on a level that was drifted through rather than attacked. ⚠ A candle this REFUSES does not kill the setup — the next qualifying pattern in the same window can still arm it. That is deliberate and is the opposite of the entry trigger, which is one-shot.")
bool   useEma  = input.bool(false, "Only trade with a higher-timeframe EMA", group = G7, tooltip = "ON = a short needs price BELOW the EMA and a long needs price ABOVE it. ⚠ Applied to the TRADE direction, never to the candle's direction — gating the pattern instead is what makes the script this idea came from take longs below its own EMA once its invert switch is on. ⚠ Expect this to remove winners as well as losers: the best fades happen at turns, and at a turn a moving average has not turned yet. It is a lagging measure filtering a leading setup, which is exactly why it is worth measuring rather than assuming.")
string emaTf   = input.timeframe("240", "   ↳ EMA timeframe", group = G7, active = useEma, tooltip = "This matters far more than the length. An EMA on the chart timeframe is basically the move you are fading — price has just swept the H4 high, so it will be above it, and the filter blocks nearly every short. On H4 or Daily it asks a different and useful question: are we selling a rally inside a bigger downtrend?")
int    emaLen  = input.int(200, "   ↳ EMA length", minval = 1, group = G7, active = useEma)
float  maxTrigPct = input.float(0.0, "Cap the trigger candle (% of stop distance, 0 = off)", minval = 0, step = 5, group = G7, tooltip = "Refuse the entry when the chart candle closed more than this far past the trigger line, measured as a percentage of the stop distance. Why it exists: the stop is pinned to the confirmation pattern's high, so a big trigger candle does not merely give a worse entry — it WIDENS the stop, and TP1 is a multiple of the stop, so the first target moves away too. Same nominal 1:1, materially lower chance of reaching it. In Aaron's worked example the close was 2.96 under the line against an 8.38 stop, about 35%. ⚠ Under the ATR stop mode this is much weaker, because there the stop no longer depends on the candle's size — only the entry price gets worse.")
float minStopPct = input.float(0.0, "Minimum stop distance (% of price, 0 = off)", minval = 0, step = 0.01, group = G7, tooltip = "Refuse a setup whose stop lands closer to the entry than this. Size is risk divided by stop distance, so a stop that collapses onto the entry does not risk less — it builds a huge position that ordinary noise removes. OFF by default so the baseline is unmeasured-and-honest; turn it on first if the equity curve looks impossible.")

// ── 8 · Chart annotations ───────────────────────────────────────
bool showLevels    = input.bool(true, "Show the liquidity levels", group = G8, tooltip = "The previous H4's high and low, drawn live and greyed once mitigated.")
bool showCC        = input.bool(true, "Show the confirmation-close line", group = G8, tooltip = "The trigger line — the confirmation candle's close. This is the line Aaron draws by hand and labels 15m.C.C.")
bool showConfLabel = input.bool(true, "Label the confirmation candle", group = G8, tooltip = "Names the pattern that armed the setup. ON by default and worth leaving on: the trend filter from the source indicator was dropped, so this build marks candles your own chart does not, and this is how you see which ones candle by candle instead of inferring it from a trade count.")
bool showTrade     = input.bool(true, "Show the risk / reward boxes", group = G8, tooltip = "Red from entry to the opening stop, green from entry to TP1, and a dashed staircase tracking the stop as the ratchet lifts it. There is no box for the runner because there is no runner target to draw one to.")
bool showBlockTag  = input.bool(true, "Mark blocked setups on chart (pink)", group = G8, tooltip = "Drops a pink 'SETUP BLOCKED' tag whenever a confirmation candle fired inside a live sweep window — the one structural fact this strategy is built on — and one of YOUR gates refused it. Hover for the reason and the price the entry would have taken. This is how you find out whether a gate is saving you money or costing it: count the tags, flip the gate, re-run, compare. Purely cosmetic — it never changes a trade. ⚠ Cheap here in a way it is not on the other strategies: a trigger can only fire once per H4 window, so the tag rate is bounded by the chart's own H4 count rather than by the bar count.")
bool logTrades     = input.bool(true, "Log every trade to Pine Logs", group = G8, tooltip = "One line per entry and per result, each tagged with the pattern that fired it. Harami and Engulfing are complements, so ONE run tagged this way answers which pattern carries the edge — no need for three runs.")


// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  THE ANNOTATION PALETTE — copied from mpc_strategy.pine, never chosen here
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ⚠ EVERY COLOUR A TRADE IS DRAWN IN IS THE A+ BOT'S (Aaron, 2026-08-12): "all those colors
// are not consistent across all the pines. They should be the same colors. Use MPC, the A+
// strategy as a standard." One result means one colour on every chart in this repo, so a
// reader moving between strategies never has to re-learn what green is. **Change a value
// here only by changing `mpc_strategy.pine` first and copying it down.**
//
// This file previously had NO colour constants at all — every value was a hex literal at its
// use site, which is why it drifted without anybody being able to see that it had. The hues
// were mostly already A+'s; the TRANSPARENCIES were not, so the same green read as a
// different shade on each file.
color POS_WIN    = color.new(#26A69A, 12)   // a closed winner's callout
color POS_LOSS   = color.new(#EF5350, 12)
color POS_BE     = color.new(#FF9800, 12)   // BREAKEVEN — see the note at the result label
color POS_DD     = color.new(#EF5350, 88)   // risk: entry → the opening stop, behind all
color POS_G1     = color.new(#26A69A, 55)   // reward: entry → TP1
color POS_STOPLN = color.new(#EF5350, 25)   // the trailing-stop staircase
color POS_GREENB = color.new(#26A69A, 0)    // solid: long entry marker
color POS_REDB   = color.new(#EF5350, 0)    // solid: short entry marker
color POS_OPENL  = color.new(#787B86, 0)    // the neutral grey — here, the trend EMA
color POS_TEXT   = color.new(#101014, 0)    // dark text on every bright label fill
// 🔴 THIS FILE HAD NO BREAKEVEN STATE AT ALL, so a +0.02R scratch drew as a full WIN and a
// −0.02R scratch as a full LOSS — the two loudest colours on the chart, for a trade that
// made nothing. Every other strategy here grades against a band and paints the middle
// orange. A+ exposes the band as an input (`execBeBandR`); this is its DEFAULT as a
// constant instead, because adding an input mid-paste resets every saved value on the
// chart and the value has never been tuned on this strategy anyway. Promote it to an input
// when the rest of this file's annotations are brought up to A+'s set.
float H4_BE_BAND = 0.15
// ⚠ THE TRIGGER LINE AND ITS LABEL ARE ORANGE, AND ORANGE IS A+'s BREAKEVEN COLOUR. That
// collision is REAL and is left alone deliberately: recolouring the trigger is a choice
// about this strategy's own chart, not a copy of A+, and A+ has no trigger to copy from.
// It is recorded in indicators/CLAUDE.md as an open question rather than silently resolved.
color TRIG_ORANGE  = color.new(#FF9800, 0)
color TRIG_ORANGEL = color.new(#FF9800, 15)
// Refusals — A+'s pink, unchanged. Added 2026-08-12 with the blocked-setup tag; this file had
// the refusal CODES since the export twin landed and nothing on the chart that drew them.
color BLK_PINK  = color.new(#FF2E9A, 12)
color BLK_PINKL = color.new(#FF2E9A, 0)
// The liquidity-level pair, already byte-identical to A+'s H4_ACTIVE_COLOR / H4_SWEPT_COLOR.
color LIQ_ACTIVE = color.new(#FF6B35, 0)
color LIQ_SWEPT  = color.new(#999999, 45)

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  1 · THE SEQUENCE
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// The ENTRY timeframe is the CHART. There is no input for it, deliberately — an input
// would be a claim the code cannot honour, since Pine cannot read a lower timeframe
// reliably. Run the chart at 5m and the entry is 5m.

// ── The three switches that turn this into a plain pattern strategy ──────────
// Added 2026-08-05 so the "Sweep and Engulf" script Aaron brought can be reproduced in
// this file instead of run beside it. All three default to the H4 sequence, so the file
// is unchanged until they are moved.
//
// ⚠ WITH `reqSweep` OFF THIS IS THE CONTROL, AND THAT IS THE POINT. The H4 gate is the
// one claim this strategy makes that a plain candlestick strategy does not. Turning it
// off and changing nothing else measures exactly what the location is worth.

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  2 · CONFIRMATION CANDLES
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Fifteen from repo32's indicator plus Sweep + Engulf, split by which side of the trade
// they can confirm. Doji appears on BOTH — it carries no direction of its own, so at a
// swept high it reads bearish and at a swept low bullish, which is the location gate
// doing the work.
// DEFAULT ON: the four per side that can actually fire on a continuous instrument.
// DEFAULT OFF: the eight that need a gap (see the header), each named so the zero is
// checkable rather than assumed.



// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  3 · RISK
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  4 · FILTERS — every one OFF by default
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Off is not timidity, it is the only way the filter can be judged. A filter that
// ships ON means the unfiltered result is never seen, so nobody can say what it was
// worth. Baseline first, then one switch at a time.

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  5 · DRAWING — none of this changes a trade
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  MARKET STRUCTURE — the canonical engine, DRAWING ONLY in this file
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Lifted BYTE-FOR-BYTE from indicators/strategies/mpc_d_strategy.pine, which lifted it from
// indicators/engines/structure_engine.pine, itself the external+internal half of mpc_assistant.pine.
// It is not re-implemented here — a second structure engine is forbidden by CLAUDE.md and
// would be the thing that silently drifts.
//
// ⚠ NOTHING BELOW THE ENGINE READS IT. This strategy trades an H4 sweep confirmed by a
// candlestick pattern; it consumes no swing, no BOS and no SOS, so this whole block draws and
// decides nothing. It is here so section 2 is the same four toggles on every chart in the repo.
// If a future rule in this file DOES start reading `st`, say so at the rule — the moment one
// does, this stops being a drawing block and the toggles stop being free.
//============================================================
//  SMC SETTINGS (hardcoded)
//============================================================
int   majorLength = 15
color bullColor   = color.blue
color bearColor   = color.red
color iBullColor  = bullColor
color iBearColor  = bearColor

//============================================================
//  MARKET STRUCTURE — input selection (mirrors mpc_assistant.pine's GRP_STRUCT)
//============================================================
string structLabelSize  = "Small"
float  pbBuffer         = 0.0

f_structSize() =>
    not showExternal ? size.auto : structLabelSize == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : structLabelSize == "Normal" ? size.normal : structLabelSize == "Large" ? size.large : structLabelSize == "Huge" ? size.huge : size.small

// Swing-point labels are hidden by making their text transparent, not by skipping
// their creation. The label objects still exist and the engine's state is untouched,
// so structure tracking, fibs, OBs and the table behave identically either way.
f_swingCol(color c) =>
    showSwingLabels ? c : color(na)

//============================================================
//  SMC STRUCTURE TYPE
//============================================================
type SMCStructure
    int    length
    float  ash             = na
    int    ash_loc         = na
    string ash_type        = ""
    line   ash_line        = na
    label  ash_lbl         = na
    float  asl             = na
    int    asl_loc         = na
    string asl_type        = ""
    line   asl_line        = na
    label  asl_lbl         = na
    float  last_conf_high     = na
    int    last_conf_high_loc = na
    float  last_conf_low      = na
    int    last_conf_low_loc  = na
    int    dir            = 0
    bool   choch_lock     = false
    line   choch_ref      = na
    int    pb_mode        = 0
    int    pb_count       = 0
    float  pb_level       = na
    float  pb_extreme     = na
    int    pb_extreme_loc = na
    line   pb_line        = na
    bool   pb_started     = false
    float  pb_last_qualify_close = na
    float  pb_last_qualify_high  = na
    float  pb_extreme_close      = na
    float  prev_close     = na
    float  prev_high      = na
    float  prev_low       = na
    bool   seeded         = false
    bool   bull_bos       = false
    float  bull_bos_high  = na
    int    bull_bos_h_loc = na
    float  bull_bos_low   = na
    int    bull_bos_l_loc = na
    bool   bear_bos       = false
    float  bear_bos_high  = na
    int    bear_bos_h_loc = na
    float  bear_bos_low   = na
    int    bear_bos_l_loc = na
    bool   new_swing_high = false
    bool   new_swing_low  = false
    bool   bull_sos       = false
    bool   bear_sos       = false

// prefix: "" for external, "i" for internal
// bull_col / bear_col allow per-instance colors
method create_ash(SMCStructure st, float val, int loc, color col, bool solid, string prefix) =>
    if not na(st.ash_line)
        line.delete(st.ash_line)
    if not na(st.ash_lbl)
        label.delete(st.ash_lbl)
        st.ash_lbl := na
    st.ash      := val
    st.ash_loc  := loc
    st.ash_type := ""
    st.ash_lbl  := label.new(loc, val, prefix + "ASH\n", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(col), style=label.style_label_down, size=f_structSize())
    st.ash_line := line.new(loc, val, bar_index, val, color=col, style=solid ? line.style_solid : line.style_dashed, width=solid ? 2 : 1)

method create_asl(SMCStructure st, float val, int loc, color col, bool solid, string prefix) =>
    if not na(st.asl_line)
        line.delete(st.asl_line)
    if not na(st.asl_lbl)
        label.delete(st.asl_lbl)
        st.asl_lbl := na
    st.asl      := val
    st.asl_loc  := loc
    st.asl_type := ""
    st.asl_lbl  := label.new(loc, val, "\n" + prefix + "ASL", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(col), style=label.style_label_up, size=f_structSize())
    st.asl_line := line.new(loc, val, bar_index, val, color=col, style=solid ? line.style_solid : line.style_dashed, width=solid ? 2 : 1)

// process() now accepts prefix + bull/bear colors so both instances share one method
method process(SMCStructure st, float ph_val, float pl_val, string prefix, color bull_col, color bear_col) =>

    st.bull_bos := false
    st.bear_bos := false
    st.new_swing_high := false
    st.new_swing_low  := false
    st.bull_sos := false
    st.bear_sos := false

    bool is_inside = false
    if not na(st.prev_high) and not na(st.prev_low)
        is_inside := high < st.prev_high and low > st.prev_low

    if st.choch_lock
        if st.dir == 1 and not na(pl_val)
            st.choch_lock := false
        else if st.dir == -1 and not na(ph_val)
            st.choch_lock := false

    if st.pb_mode == 1
        if not st.pb_started
            st.pb_started            := true
            st.pb_extreme            := high
            st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
            st.pb_extreme_close      := na
            st.pb_count              := 0
            st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
        else
            bool extreme_updated_1 = false
            if na(st.pb_extreme) or high > st.pb_extreme
                st.pb_extreme            := high
                st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
                st.pb_extreme_close      := na
                st.pb_count              := 0
                st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
                st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
                extreme_updated_1        := true
            bool extreme_is_bearish_1 = extreme_updated_1 and close < open
            bool is_candle1_1 = na(st.pb_last_qualify_close) and not extreme_updated_1
            if (not is_inside or is_candle1_1) and (not extreme_updated_1 or extreme_is_bearish_1)
                float threshold = na(st.pb_last_qualify_high) ? st.pb_extreme : st.pb_last_qualify_high
                if close < threshold - pbBuffer
                    st.pb_count              += 1
                    st.pb_last_qualify_close := close
                    st.pb_last_qualify_high  := low
            if st.pb_count >= 3 and not na(st.pb_extreme) and not na(st.pb_extreme_loc)
                if not na(st.ash_line)
                    line.delete(st.ash_line)
                if not na(st.ash_lbl)
                    label.delete(st.ash_lbl)
                st.ash      := st.pb_extreme
                st.ash_loc  := st.pb_extreme_loc
                st.ash_type := "LOCKED"
                st.ash_line := line.new(st.pb_extreme_loc, st.pb_extreme, bar_index, st.pb_extreme, color=bear_col, style=line.style_solid, width=1)
                st.ash_lbl  := label.new(st.pb_extreme_loc, st.pb_extreme, prefix + "ASH\n", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(bear_col), style=label.style_label_down, size=f_structSize())
                st.new_swing_high := true
                st.pb_mode    := 0
                st.pb_count   := 0
                st.choch_lock := false

    else if st.pb_mode == -1
        if not st.pb_started
            st.pb_started            := true
            st.pb_extreme            := low
            st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
            st.pb_extreme_close      := na
            st.pb_count              := 0
            st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
        else
            bool extreme_updated_m1 = false
            if na(st.pb_extreme) or low < st.pb_extreme
                st.pb_extreme            := low
                st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
                st.pb_extreme_close      := na
                st.pb_count              := 0
                st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
                st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
                extreme_updated_m1       := true
            bool extreme_is_bullish_m1 = extreme_updated_m1 and close > open
            bool is_candle1_m1 = na(st.pb_last_qualify_close) and not extreme_updated_m1
            if (not is_inside or is_candle1_m1) and (not extreme_updated_m1 or extreme_is_bullish_m1)
                float threshold = na(st.pb_last_qualify_high) ? st.pb_extreme : st.pb_last_qualify_high
                if close > threshold + pbBuffer
                    st.pb_count              += 1
                    st.pb_last_qualify_close := close
                    st.pb_last_qualify_high  := high
            if st.pb_count >= 3 and not na(st.pb_extreme) and not na(st.pb_extreme_loc)
                if not na(st.asl_line)
                    line.delete(st.asl_line)
                if not na(st.asl_lbl)
                    label.delete(st.asl_lbl)
                st.asl      := st.pb_extreme
                st.asl_loc  := st.pb_extreme_loc
                st.asl_type := "LOCKED"
                st.asl_line := line.new(st.pb_extreme_loc, st.pb_extreme, bar_index, st.pb_extreme, color=bull_col, style=line.style_solid, width=1)
                st.asl_lbl  := label.new(st.pb_extreme_loc, st.pb_extreme, "\n" + prefix + "ASL", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(bull_col), style=label.style_label_up, size=f_structSize())
                st.new_swing_low := true
                st.pb_mode    := 0
                st.pb_count   := 0
                st.choch_lock := false

    st.prev_close := close
    st.prev_high  := high
    st.prev_low   := low

    if na(st.ash) and na(st.asl) and not st.seeded
        if not na(ph_val)
            st.create_ash(ph_val, bar_index[st.length], bear_col, false, prefix)
            st.dir := -1
        else if not na(pl_val)
            st.create_asl(pl_val, bar_index[st.length], bull_col, false, prefix)
            st.dir := 1

    if not st.seeded
        if not na(st.ash) and na(st.asl)
            float seed_low = low
            int   seed_loc = bar_index
            int   lb       = math.min(bar_index, 500)
            for i = 0 to lb
                if low[i] < seed_low
                    seed_low := low[i]
                    seed_loc := bar_index - i
            if seed_low < st.ash
                st.asl      := seed_low
                st.asl_loc  := seed_loc
                st.asl_type := ""
                st.asl_line := line.new(seed_loc, seed_low, bar_index, seed_low, color=bull_col, style=line.style_dashed, width=1)
                st.asl_lbl  := label.new(seed_loc, seed_low, "\n" + prefix + "ASL", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(bull_col), style=label.style_label_up, size=f_structSize())
                st.seeded := true
        else if not na(st.asl) and na(st.ash)
            float seed_high = high
            int   seed_loc  = bar_index
            int   lb        = math.min(bar_index, 500)
            for i = 0 to lb
                if high[i] > seed_high
                    seed_high := high[i]
                    seed_loc  := bar_index - i
            if seed_high > st.asl
                st.ash      := seed_high
                st.ash_loc  := seed_loc
                st.ash_type := ""
                st.ash_line := line.new(seed_loc, seed_high, bar_index, seed_high, color=bear_col, style=line.style_dashed, width=1)
                st.ash_lbl  := label.new(seed_loc, seed_high, prefix + "ASH\n", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(bear_col), style=label.style_label_down, size=f_structSize())
                st.seeded := true
        else if not na(st.ash) and not na(st.asl)
            st.seeded := true

    if na(st.last_conf_high) and na(st.last_conf_low)
        if not na(ph_val) and not na(st.ash) and st.ash_type == "" and st.pb_mode == 0
            if ph_val > st.ash
                st.create_ash(ph_val, bar_index[st.length], bear_col, false, prefix)
        if not na(pl_val) and not na(st.asl) and st.asl_type == "" and st.pb_mode == 0
            if pl_val < st.asl
                st.create_asl(pl_val, bar_index[st.length], bull_col, false, prefix)

    bool ash_broken = not na(st.ash) and close > st.ash
    bool asl_broken = not na(st.asl) and close < st.asl

    if ash_broken
        st.bull_bos := true
        st.bull_bos_high  := st.ash
        st.bull_bos_h_loc := st.ash_loc

        bool was_in_bear_pb = st.pb_mode == -1 and not na(st.pb_extreme) and not na(st.pb_extreme_loc)
        st.pb_mode  := 0
        st.pb_count := 0

        bool   is_choch    = st.dir == -1
        string brk_lbl_txt = is_choch ? prefix + "SOS" : prefix + "BOS"
        if is_choch
            st.bull_sos := true
        int    mid_x       = math.round((st.ash_loc + bar_index) / 2)
        label.new(mid_x, st.ash, "\n" + brk_lbl_txt, color=color(na), textcolor=bull_col, style=label.style_label_down, size=size.tiny)

        if is_choch
            st.choch_lock := true

        bool brk_already_conf_high = (st.ash == st.last_conf_high and st.ash_loc == st.last_conf_high_loc)
        if not na(st.ash_lbl)
            label.delete(st.ash_lbl)
        if not brk_already_conf_high
            bool   brk_is_hh  = na(st.last_conf_high) or st.ash >= st.last_conf_high
            string brk_high_t = brk_is_hh ? prefix + "HH" : prefix + "LH"
            color  brk_high_c = brk_is_hh ? bull_col : bear_col
            label.new(st.ash_loc, st.ash, brk_high_t + "\n", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(brk_high_c), style=label.style_label_down, size=f_structSize())

        if not na(st.ash_line)
            line.set_style(st.ash_line, line.style_solid)
            line.set_color(st.ash_line, bull_col)
            line.set_width(st.ash_line, 2)
            line.set_x2(st.ash_line, bar_index)
            st.ash_line := na

        st.last_conf_high     := st.ash
        st.last_conf_high_loc := st.ash_loc
        st.ash_lbl            := na
        st.ash                := na
        st.dir                := 1

        if was_in_bear_pb
            st.bull_bos_low   := st.pb_extreme
            st.bull_bos_l_loc := st.pb_extreme_loc
            if not na(st.asl_line)
                line.delete(st.asl_line)
            if not na(st.asl_lbl)
                label.delete(st.asl_lbl)
            bool   pb_is_hl = is_choch ? false : (na(st.last_conf_low) or st.pb_extreme >= st.last_conf_low)
            // On an SOS (fast reversal) the extreme is only the ACTIVE swing low —
            // it prints as ASL and is confirmed to HL/LL by the NEXT bullish break.
            string pb_low_t = is_choch ? prefix + "ASL" : (pb_is_hl ? prefix + "HL" : prefix + "LL")
            color  pb_low_c = is_choch ? bull_col : (pb_is_hl ? bull_col : bear_col)
            st.asl      := st.pb_extreme
            st.asl_loc  := st.pb_extreme_loc
            st.asl_type := "LOCKED"
            st.asl_line := line.new(st.pb_extreme_loc, st.pb_extreme, bar_index, st.pb_extreme, color=bull_col, style=line.style_solid, width=1)
            st.asl_lbl  := label.new(st.pb_extreme_loc, st.pb_extreme, "\n" + pb_low_t, color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(pb_low_c), style=label.style_label_up, size=f_structSize())
            if not is_choch
                st.last_conf_low     := st.pb_extreme
                st.last_conf_low_loc := st.pb_extreme_loc
            st.pb_extreme            := high
            st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
            st.pb_extreme_close      := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
            st.pb_started            := true
            st.pb_count              := 0
            st.pb_level              := na
            st.pb_mode               := 1
            st.pb_started            := true
        else
            if not na(st.asl)
                bool already_conf_low = (st.asl == st.last_conf_low and st.asl_loc == st.last_conf_low_loc)
                if not already_conf_low
                    bool   old_is_hl = is_choch ? false : (na(st.last_conf_low) or st.asl >= st.last_conf_low)
                    string old_low_t = old_is_hl ? prefix + "HL" : prefix + "LL"
                    color  old_low_c = old_is_hl ? bull_col : bear_col
                    if not na(st.asl_lbl)
                        label.delete(st.asl_lbl)
                    label.new(st.asl_loc, st.asl, "\n" + old_low_t, color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(old_low_c), style=label.style_label_up, size=f_structSize())
                    st.last_conf_low     := st.asl
                    st.last_conf_low_loc := st.asl_loc
                else
                    if not na(st.asl_lbl)
                        label.delete(st.asl_lbl)
                if not na(st.asl_line)
                    line.delete(st.asl_line)
                st.asl_line := na
                st.asl_lbl  := na
                st.asl      := na

            float lowest_val = low
            int   lowest_loc = bar_index
            int   bars_back  = na(st.last_conf_high_loc) ? bar_index : bar_index - st.last_conf_high_loc
            if bars_back > 0
                int max_lb = math.min(math.min(bars_back, 1490), bar_index)
                for i = 0 to max_lb
                    if low[i] < lowest_val
                        lowest_val := low[i]
                        lowest_loc := bar_index - i

            st.bull_bos_low   := lowest_val
            st.bull_bos_l_loc := lowest_loc

            st.asl      := lowest_val
            st.asl_loc  := lowest_loc
            st.asl_type := ""
            st.asl_line := line.new(lowest_loc, lowest_val, bar_index, lowest_val, color=bull_col, style=line.style_solid, width=1)
            if lowest_val != st.last_conf_low
                st.asl_lbl := label.new(lowest_loc, lowest_val, "\n" + prefix + "ASL", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(bull_col), style=label.style_label_up, size=f_structSize())
            else
                st.asl_lbl := na

            st.pb_mode               := 1
            st.pb_count              := 0
            st.pb_level              := na
            st.pb_extreme            := high
            st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
            st.pb_extreme_close      := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
            st.pb_started            := true

    else if asl_broken
        st.bear_bos := true
        st.bear_bos_low   := st.asl
        st.bear_bos_l_loc := st.asl_loc

        bool was_in_bull_pb = st.pb_mode == 1 and not na(st.pb_extreme) and not na(st.pb_extreme_loc)
        st.pb_mode  := 0
        st.pb_count := 0

        bool   is_choch    = st.dir == 1
        string brk_lbl_txt = is_choch ? prefix + "SOS" : prefix + "BOS"
        if is_choch
            st.bear_sos := true
        int    mid_x       = math.round((st.asl_loc + bar_index) / 2)
        label.new(mid_x, st.asl, brk_lbl_txt + "\n", color=color(na), textcolor=bear_col, style=label.style_label_up, size=size.tiny)

        if is_choch
            st.choch_lock := true

        bool brk_already_conf_low = (st.asl == st.last_conf_low and st.asl_loc == st.last_conf_low_loc)
        if not na(st.asl_lbl)
            label.delete(st.asl_lbl)
        if not brk_already_conf_low
            bool   brk_is_hl = na(st.last_conf_low) or st.asl >= st.last_conf_low
            string brk_low_t = brk_is_hl ? prefix + "HL" : prefix + "LL"
            label.new(st.asl_loc, st.asl, "\n" + brk_low_t, color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(bear_col), style=label.style_label_up, size=f_structSize())

        if not na(st.asl_line)
            line.set_style(st.asl_line, line.style_solid)
            line.set_color(st.asl_line, bear_col)
            line.set_width(st.asl_line, 2)
            line.set_x2(st.asl_line, bar_index)
            st.asl_line := na

        st.last_conf_low     := st.asl
        st.last_conf_low_loc := st.asl_loc
        st.asl_lbl           := na
        st.asl               := na
        st.dir               := -1

        if was_in_bull_pb
            st.bear_bos_high  := st.pb_extreme
            st.bear_bos_h_loc := st.pb_extreme_loc
            if not na(st.ash_line)
                line.delete(st.ash_line)
            if not na(st.ash_lbl)
                label.delete(st.ash_lbl)
            bool   pb_is_hh  = na(st.last_conf_high) or st.pb_extreme >= st.last_conf_high
            // On an SOS (fast reversal) the extreme is only the ACTIVE swing high —
            // it prints as ASH and is confirmed to HH/LH by the NEXT bearish break.
            string pb_high_t = is_choch ? prefix + "ASH" : (pb_is_hh ? prefix + "HH" : prefix + "LH")
            color  pb_high_c = is_choch ? bear_col : (pb_is_hh ? bull_col : bear_col)
            st.ash      := st.pb_extreme
            st.ash_loc  := st.pb_extreme_loc
            st.ash_type := "LOCKED"
            st.ash_line := line.new(st.pb_extreme_loc, st.pb_extreme, bar_index, st.pb_extreme, color=bear_col, style=line.style_solid, width=1)
            st.ash_lbl  := label.new(st.pb_extreme_loc, st.pb_extreme, pb_high_t + "\n", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(pb_high_c), style=label.style_label_down, size=f_structSize())
            if not is_choch
                st.last_conf_high     := st.pb_extreme
                st.last_conf_high_loc := st.pb_extreme_loc
            st.pb_extreme            := low
            st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
            st.pb_extreme_close      := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
            st.pb_started            := true
            st.pb_count              := 0
            st.pb_level              := na
            st.pb_mode               := -1
            st.pb_started            := true
        else
            float highest_val = high
            int   highest_loc = bar_index
            int   bars_back   = na(st.last_conf_low_loc) ? bar_index : bar_index - st.last_conf_low_loc
            if bars_back > 0
                int max_lb = math.min(math.min(bars_back, 1490), bar_index)
                for i = 0 to max_lb
                    if high[i] > highest_val
                        highest_val := high[i]
                        highest_loc := bar_index - i

            if not na(st.ash)
                bool already_conf_high = (st.ash == st.last_conf_high and st.ash_loc == st.last_conf_high_loc)
                if not already_conf_high
                    bool   old_is_hh  = is_choch ? true : (na(st.last_conf_high) or st.ash >= st.last_conf_high)
                    string old_high_t = old_is_hh ? prefix + "HH" : prefix + "LH"
                    color  old_high_c = old_is_hh ? bull_col : bear_col
                    if not na(st.ash_lbl)
                        label.delete(st.ash_lbl)
                    label.new(st.ash_loc, st.ash, old_high_t + "\n", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(old_high_c), style=label.style_label_down, size=f_structSize())
                    st.last_conf_high     := st.ash
                    st.last_conf_high_loc := st.ash_loc
                else
                    if not na(st.ash_lbl)
                        label.delete(st.ash_lbl)
                if not na(st.ash_line)
                    line.delete(st.ash_line)
                st.ash_line := na
                st.ash_lbl  := na
                st.ash      := na
            else
                // Neither an active pullback high nor a confirmed ASH was available to
                // promote — use the actual highest point since the last confirmed low so
                // a genuine swing high still gets confirmed instead of silently vanishing.
                bool   fallback_is_hh  = na(st.last_conf_high) or highest_val >= st.last_conf_high
                string fallback_high_t = fallback_is_hh ? prefix + "HH" : prefix + "LH"
                color  fallback_high_c = fallback_is_hh ? bull_col : bear_col
                if highest_val != st.last_conf_high
                    label.new(highest_loc, highest_val, fallback_high_t + "\n", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(fallback_high_c), style=label.style_label_down, size=f_structSize())
                    st.last_conf_high     := highest_val
                    st.last_conf_high_loc := highest_loc

            st.bear_bos_high  := highest_val
            st.bear_bos_h_loc := highest_loc

            st.ash      := highest_val
            st.ash_loc  := highest_loc
            st.ash_type := ""
            st.ash_line := line.new(highest_loc, highest_val, bar_index, highest_val, color=bear_col, style=line.style_solid, width=1)
            if highest_val != st.last_conf_high
                st.ash_lbl := label.new(highest_loc, highest_val, prefix + "ASH\n", color=color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(bear_col), style=label.style_label_down, size=f_structSize())
            else
                st.ash_lbl := na

            st.pb_mode               := -1
            st.pb_count              := 0
            st.pb_level              := na
            st.pb_extreme            := low
            st.pb_extreme_loc        := bar_index
            st.pb_extreme_close      := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_close := na
            st.pb_last_qualify_high  := na
            st.pb_started            := true

    if not na(st.ash_line)
        line.set_x2(st.ash_line, bar_index)
        if not showExternal
            line.set_color(st.ash_line, color(na))
    if not na(st.asl_line)
        line.set_x2(st.asl_line, bar_index)
        if not showExternal
            line.set_color(st.asl_line, color(na))
    if not showExternal
        if not na(st.ash_lbl)
            label.set_textcolor(st.ash_lbl, color(na))
        if not na(st.asl_lbl)
            label.set_textcolor(st.asl_lbl, color(na))

//============================================================
//  EXECUTION — EXTERNAL STRUCTURE
//============================================================
// External structure engine — majorLength=15, blue/red, prefix ""
var st = SMCStructure.new(majorLength)
ph = ta.pivothigh(high, majorLength, majorLength)
pl = ta.pivotlow(low,  majorLength, majorLength)
// showExternal off → pass color(na) so ALL lines and labels hidden inside process
// showExternal off but showExternal on → pass color(na) for labels only — handled via ASH/ASL override below
color extBullCol = showExternal ? (showExternal ? bullColor : color(na)) : color(na)
color extBearCol = showExternal ? (showExternal ? bearColor : color(na)) : color(na)
st.process(ph, pl, "", extBullCol, extBearCol)

// After process runs — restore line colors when labels are hidden but structure is visible
if not na(st.ash_line)
    line.set_x2(st.ash_line, bar_index)
    if showExternal and not showExternal
        line.set_color(st.ash_line, bullColor)
if not na(st.asl_line)
    line.set_x2(st.asl_line, bar_index)
    if showExternal and not showExternal
        line.set_color(st.asl_line, bearColor)
if not na(st.ash_lbl)
    label.set_textcolor(st.ash_lbl, showExternal ? f_swingCol(bearColor) : color(na))
if not na(st.asl_lbl)
    label.set_textcolor(st.asl_lbl, showExternal ? f_swingCol(bullColor) : color(na))

//============================================================
//  EXECUTION — INTERNAL STRUCTURE
//============================================================
// Internal structure — Step 2: pullback tracking to confirm iSH / iSL

// ── State ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
var int   i_mode           = 0
var bool  i_seeded         = false

// Pullback tracking
var float i_pb_extreme     = na
var int   i_pb_extreme_loc = na
var int   i_pb_count       = 0
var bool  i_pb_started     = false
var float i_pb_lqc         = na
var float i_pb_lqh         = na
var float i_prev_high      = na
var float i_prev_low       = na

// Active swing level (iSH or iSL)
var float i_sw_price       = na
var int   i_sw_loc         = na
var line  i_sw_line        = na
var label i_sw_lbl         = na

// Pre-declared locals (Pine v6)
var bool  i_ext_chg        = false
var bool  i_is_inside      = false
var bool  i_ext_dir        = false
var bool  i_is_c1          = false
var float i_thresh         = na

var float i_tracked_ext     = na
var int   i_tracked_ext_loc = na
var int   i_last_mode       = 0   // remembers what mode confirmed the swing
var bool  i_had_bos         = false
var int   i_bos_dir         = 0
var string i_h_lbl          = ""
var color  i_h_col          = color.black
var string i_l_lbl          = ""
var color  i_l_col          = color.black
var int   i_mid             = 0
var int   i_mid2            = 0
var float i_last_hl         = na   // last confirmed iHL price (for iSOS in bullish cycle)

var float i_last_lh         = na   // last confirmed iLH price (for iSOS in bearish cycle)
var int   i_last_hl_loc     = na
var int   i_last_lh_loc     = na

var float i_sos_watch_hh    = na
var int   i_sos_watch_hh_loc= na
var float i_sos_watch_ll    = na
var int   i_sos_watch_ll_loc= na

float i_lbl_y_offset = syminfo.mintick * 20   // vertical offset for iBOS/iSOS (smaller number = closer to the line)

// Internal structure is naturally scoped to the current active external swing —
// it resets on every external SOS/CHoCH (see block right below).
bool internalActive = showInternal

// Tracks every internal-structure label/line drawn during the current external
// swing, so they can be wiped when a new swing starts (unless showHistoricalInternal is on).
var array<label> intHistLabels = array.new<label>()
var array<line>  intHistLines  = array.new<line>()

// ── Stop internal tracking on external SOS ───────────────

if internalActive and (st.bull_bos or st.bear_bos or st.bull_sos or st.bear_sos)
    if not na(i_sw_line)
        line.set_x2(i_sw_line, bar_index)
        i_sw_line := na
    i_sw_lbl          := na
    i_sw_price        := na
    i_mode            := 0
    i_seeded          := false
    i_pb_count        := 0
    i_pb_started      := false
    i_tracked_ext     := na
    i_tracked_ext_loc := na
    i_last_hl         := na
    i_last_lh         := na
    i_had_bos         := false
    i_sos_watch_hh    := na
    i_sos_watch_ll    := na
    // Past swing just ended — wipe its internal structure unless history is enabled
    if not showHistoricalInternal
        if array.size(intHistLabels) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(intHistLabels) - 1
                label.delete(array.get(intHistLabels, i))
        if array.size(intHistLines) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(intHistLines) - 1
                line.delete(array.get(intHistLines, i))
    array.clear(intHistLabels)
    array.clear(intHistLines)

// ── Track prev bar ────────────────────────────────────────
if internalActive
    i_prev_high := high
    i_prev_low  := low


// ── Seed on new external swing ────────────────────────────
if internalActive
    if st.new_swing_low and not st.bull_sos and not st.bear_sos
        i_mode            := 1
        i_seeded          := true
        i_had_bos         := false
        i_bos_dir         := 0
        i_pb_started      := false
        i_pb_extreme      := na
        i_pb_count        := 0
        i_pb_lqc          := na
        i_pb_lqh          := na
        i_tracked_ext     := na
        i_tracked_ext_loc := na
        i_last_mode       := 1
        i_last_hl         := na
        i_last_lh         := na
        i_sos_watch_hh    := na
        i_sos_watch_ll    := na
    else if st.new_swing_high and not st.bull_sos and not st.bear_sos
        i_mode            := -1
        i_seeded          := true
        i_had_bos         := false
        i_bos_dir         := 0
        i_pb_started      := false
        i_pb_extreme      := na
        i_pb_count        := 0
        i_pb_lqc          := na
        i_pb_lqh          := na
        i_tracked_ext     := na
        i_tracked_ext_loc := na
        i_last_mode       := -1
        i_last_hl         := na
        i_last_lh         := na
        i_sos_watch_hh    := na
        i_sos_watch_ll    := na

// ── Mode 1: track upward move → confirm iSH ──────────────
if internalActive and i_seeded and i_mode == 1
    if not i_pb_started
        i_pb_started     := true
        i_pb_extreme     := high
        i_pb_extreme_loc := bar_index
        i_pb_count       := 0
        i_pb_lqc         := na
        i_pb_lqh         := na
    else
        // Update extreme if new high
        i_ext_chg := false
        if high > i_pb_extreme
            i_pb_extreme     := high
            i_pb_extreme_loc := bar_index
            i_pb_count       := 0
            i_pb_lqc         := na
            i_pb_lqh         := na
            i_ext_chg        := true
        // is_inside and qualifying bar checks (exact external rule)
        i_is_inside := not na(i_prev_high) and not na(i_prev_low) and high < i_prev_high and low > i_prev_low
        i_ext_dir   := i_ext_chg and close < open
        i_is_c1     := na(i_pb_lqc) and not i_ext_chg
        if (not i_is_inside or i_is_c1) and (not i_ext_chg or i_ext_dir)
            i_thresh := na(i_pb_lqh) ? i_pb_extreme : i_pb_lqh
            if close < i_thresh - pbBuffer
                i_pb_count += 1
                i_pb_lqc   := close
                i_pb_lqh   := low
        // 3 bars confirmed → iSH
        if i_pb_count >= 3 and not na(i_pb_extreme)
            if not na(i_sw_line)
                line.set_x2(i_sw_line, bar_index)
            i_sw_line  := na
            i_sw_lbl   := na
            i_sw_price := i_pb_extreme
            i_sw_loc   := i_pb_extreme_loc
            // Label: iSH if first swing, iHH if higher than last, iLH if lower
            i_h_lbl := not i_had_bos ? "iSH" : "iHH"
            i_h_col := not i_had_bos ? iBearColor : iBullColor
            i_sw_line  := line.new(i_sw_loc, i_sw_price, bar_index, i_sw_price, color = showInternal ? color.new(i_h_col, 15) : color(na), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
            i_sw_lbl   := label.new(i_sw_loc, i_sw_price, i_h_lbl + "\n", color = color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(color.new(i_h_col, 15)), style = label.style_label_down, size = size.tiny)
            array.push(intHistLines, i_sw_line)
            array.push(intHistLabels, i_sw_lbl)
            i_mode       := 0
            i_pb_count   := 0
            i_pb_started := false

// ── Mode -1: track downward move → confirm iSL ───────────
if internalActive and i_seeded and i_mode == -1
    if not i_pb_started
        i_pb_started     := true
        i_pb_extreme     := low
        i_pb_extreme_loc := bar_index
        i_pb_count       := 0
        i_pb_lqc         := na
        i_pb_lqh         := na
    else
        // Update extreme if new low
        i_ext_chg := false
        if low < i_pb_extreme
            i_pb_extreme     := low
            i_pb_extreme_loc := bar_index
            i_pb_count       := 0
            i_pb_lqc         := na
            i_pb_lqh         := na
            i_ext_chg        := true
        // is_inside and qualifying bar checks
        i_is_inside := not na(i_prev_high) and not na(i_prev_low) and high < i_prev_high and low > i_prev_low
        i_ext_dir   := i_ext_chg and close > open
        i_is_c1     := na(i_pb_lqc) and not i_ext_chg
        if (not i_is_inside or i_is_c1) and (not i_ext_chg or i_ext_dir)
            i_thresh := na(i_pb_lqh) ? i_pb_extreme : i_pb_lqh
            if close > i_thresh + pbBuffer
                i_pb_count += 1
                i_pb_lqc   := close
                i_pb_lqh   := high
        // 3 bars confirmed → iSL
        if i_pb_count >= 3 and not na(i_pb_extreme)
            if not na(i_sw_line)
                line.set_x2(i_sw_line, bar_index)
            i_sw_line  := na
            i_sw_lbl   := na
            i_sw_price := i_pb_extreme
            i_sw_loc   := i_pb_extreme_loc
            // Label: iSL if first swing, iLL if lower than last, iHL if higher
            i_l_lbl := not i_had_bos ? "iSL" : "iLL"
            i_l_col := not i_had_bos ? iBullColor : iBearColor
            i_sw_line  := line.new(i_sw_loc, i_sw_price, bar_index, i_sw_price, color = showInternal ? color.new(i_l_col, 15) : color(na), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
            i_sw_lbl   := label.new(i_sw_loc, i_sw_price, "\n" + i_l_lbl, color = color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(color.new(i_l_col, 15)), style = label.style_label_up, size = size.tiny)
            array.push(intHistLines, i_sw_line)
            array.push(intHistLabels, i_sw_lbl)
            i_mode       := 0
            i_pb_count   := 0
            i_pb_started := false

// ── Track extreme while watching (mode 0) ────────────────
if internalActive and i_seeded and i_mode == 0
    if i_last_mode == 1
        if na(i_tracked_ext) or low < i_tracked_ext
            i_tracked_ext     := low
            i_tracked_ext_loc := bar_index
    else if i_last_mode == -1
        if na(i_tracked_ext) or high > i_tracked_ext
            i_tracked_ext     := high
            i_tracked_ext_loc := bar_index

// ── iBOS / iSOS detection ────────────────────────────────
bool int_bull_break = false
bool int_bear_break = false
bool int_bull_bos   = false
bool int_bull_sos   = false
bool int_bear_bos   = false
bool int_bear_sos   = false
int  int_break_origin_loc = na

if internalActive and i_mode == 0 and i_seeded and not na(i_sw_price) and barstate.isconfirmed
    if close > i_sw_price and i_last_mode == 1
        i_mid := math.round((i_sw_loc + bar_index) / 2)
        label iBullBOSLbl = label.new(i_mid, i_sw_price + i_lbl_y_offset, "iBOS", color = color(na), textcolor = showInternal ? iBullColor : color(na), style = label.style_none, size = size.tiny, textalign = text.align_center)
        array.push(intHistLabels, iBullBOSLbl)
        if not na(i_sw_line)
            line.set_x2(i_sw_line, bar_index)
            i_sw_line := na
        i_sw_lbl := na
        if not na(i_tracked_ext)
            line  iHLLine = line.new(i_tracked_ext_loc, i_tracked_ext, bar_index, i_tracked_ext, color = showInternal ? color.new(iBullColor, 15) : color(na), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
            label iHLLbl  = label.new(i_tracked_ext_loc, i_tracked_ext, "\niHL", color = color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(color.new(iBullColor, 15)), style = label.style_label_up, size = size.tiny)
            array.push(intHistLines, iHLLine)
            array.push(intHistLabels, iHLLbl)
            i_last_hl     := i_tracked_ext
            i_last_hl_loc := i_tracked_ext_loc
        
        int_bull_break := true
        int_bull_bos   := true
        int_break_origin_loc := i_tracked_ext_loc

        i_sw_price       := na
        i_tracked_ext    := na
        i_tracked_ext_loc := na
        i_pb_count       := 0
        i_pb_started     := false
        i_pb_lqc         := na
        i_pb_lqh         := na
        i_had_bos        := true
        i_bos_dir        := 1
        i_last_mode      := 1
        i_mode           := 1
        i_sos_watch_ll   := na

    else if close < i_sw_price and i_last_mode == -1
        i_mid2 := math.round((i_sw_loc + bar_index) / 2)
        label iBearBOSLbl = label.new(i_mid2, i_sw_price, "iBOS", color = color(na), textcolor = showInternal ? iBearColor : color(na), style = label.style_label_up, size = size.tiny, textalign = text.align_center)
        array.push(intHistLabels, iBearBOSLbl)
        if not na(i_sw_line)
            line.set_x2(i_sw_line, bar_index)
            i_sw_line := na
        i_sw_lbl := na
        if not na(i_tracked_ext)
            line  iLHLine = line.new(i_tracked_ext_loc, i_tracked_ext, bar_index, i_tracked_ext, color = showInternal ? color.new(iBearColor, 15) : color(na), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
            label iLHLbl  = label.new(i_tracked_ext_loc, i_tracked_ext, "iLH\n", color = color(na), textcolor=f_swingCol(color.new(iBearColor, 15)), style = label.style_label_down, size = size.tiny)
            array.push(intHistLines, iLHLine)
            array.push(intHistLabels, iLHLbl)
            i_last_lh     := i_tracked_ext
            i_last_lh_loc := i_tracked_ext_loc
            
        int_bear_break := true
        int_bear_bos   := true
        int_break_origin_loc := i_tracked_ext_loc

        i_sw_price        := na
        i_tracked_ext     := na
        i_tracked_ext_loc := na
        i_pb_count        := 0
        i_pb_started      := false
        i_pb_lqc          := na
        i_pb_lqh          := na
        i_had_bos         := true
        i_bos_dir         := -1
        i_last_mode       := -1
        i_mode            := -1
        i_sos_watch_hh    := na



// ── iSOS detection (watches last iHL / iLH) ──────────────
if internalActive and i_seeded and i_had_bos and barstate.isconfirmed
    if i_last_mode == 1 and not na(i_last_hl) and close < i_last_hl and i_mode == 0
        i_mid2 := math.round((i_last_hl_loc + bar_index) / 2)
        label iSOS1Lbl = label.new(i_mid2, i_last_hl, "iSOS", color = color(na), textcolor = showInternal ? iBearColor : color(na), style = label.style_label_up, size = size.tiny, textalign = text.align_center)
        line  iSOS1Line = line.new(i_last_hl_loc, i_last_hl, bar_index, i_last_hl, color = showInternal ? color.new(iBearColor, 15) : color(na), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
        array.push(intHistLabels, iSOS1Lbl)
        array.push(intHistLines, iSOS1Line)
        if not na(i_sw_line)
            line.set_x2(i_sw_line, bar_index)
            i_sw_line := na
        
        i_sos_watch_hh     := i_sw_price
        i_sos_watch_hh_loc := i_sw_loc
        i_sos_watch_ll     := na
        
        int_bear_break := true
        int_bear_sos   := true
        int_break_origin_loc := i_sw_loc

        i_sw_lbl          := na
        i_sw_price        := na
        i_tracked_ext     := na
        i_tracked_ext_loc := na
        i_last_hl         := na
        i_pb_count        := 0
        i_pb_started      := false
        i_pb_lqc          := na
        i_pb_lqh          := na
        i_last_mode       := -1
        i_mode            := -1

    else if i_last_mode == -1 and not na(i_last_lh) and close > i_last_lh and i_mode == 0
        i_mid := math.round((i_last_lh_loc + bar_index) / 2)
        label iSOS2Lbl = label.new(i_mid, i_last_lh + i_lbl_y_offset, "iSOS", color = color(na), textcolor = showInternal ? iBullColor : color(na), style = label.style_none, size = size.tiny, textalign = text.align_center)
        line  iSOS2Line = line.new(i_last_lh_loc, i_last_lh, bar_index, i_last_lh, color = showInternal ? color.new(iBullColor, 15) : color(na), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
        array.push(intHistLabels, iSOS2Lbl)
        array.push(intHistLines, iSOS2Line)
        if not na(i_sw_line)
            line.set_x2(i_sw_line, bar_index)
            i_sw_line := na
            
        i_sos_watch_ll     := i_sw_price
        i_sos_watch_ll_loc := i_sw_loc
        i_sos_watch_hh     := na
        
        int_bull_break := true
        int_bull_sos   := true
        int_break_origin_loc := i_sw_loc

        i_sw_lbl          := na
        i_sw_price        := na
        i_tracked_ext     := na
        i_tracked_ext_loc := na
        i_last_lh         := na
        i_pb_count        := 0
        i_pb_started      := false
        i_pb_lqc          := na
        i_pb_lqh          := na
        i_last_mode       := 1
        i_mode            := 1

    else if i_last_mode == -1 and not na(i_sos_watch_hh) and close > i_sos_watch_hh and i_mode == 0
        i_mid := math.round((i_sos_watch_hh_loc + bar_index) / 2)
        label iSOS3Lbl = label.new(i_mid, i_sos_watch_hh + i_lbl_y_offset, "iSOS", color = color(na), textcolor = showInternal ? iBullColor : color(na), style = label.style_none, size = size.tiny, textalign = text.align_center)
        line  iSOS3Line = line.new(i_sos_watch_hh_loc, i_sos_watch_hh, bar_index, i_sos_watch_hh, color = showInternal ? color.new(iBullColor, 15) : color(na), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
        array.push(intHistLabels, iSOS3Lbl)
        array.push(intHistLines, iSOS3Line)
        if not na(i_sw_line)
            line.set_x2(i_sw_line, bar_index)
            i_sw_line := na
            
        i_sos_watch_ll     := i_sw_price
        i_sos_watch_ll_loc := i_sw_loc
        
        int_bull_break := true
        int_bull_sos   := true
        int_break_origin_loc := i_sw_loc

        i_sw_lbl          := na
        i_sw_price        := na
        i_tracked_ext     := na
        i_tracked_ext_loc := na
        i_last_lh         := na
        i_pb_count        := 0
        i_pb_started      := false
        i_pb_lqc          := na
        i_pb_lqh          := na
        i_last_mode       := 1
        i_mode            := 1
        i_sos_watch_hh    := na

    else if i_last_mode == 1 and not na(i_sos_watch_ll) and close < i_sos_watch_ll and i_mode == 0
        i_mid2 := math.round((i_sos_watch_ll_loc + bar_index) / 2)
        label iSOS4Lbl = label.new(i_mid2, i_sos_watch_ll, "iSOS", color = color(na), textcolor = showInternal ? iBearColor : color(na), style = label.style_label_up, size = size.tiny, textalign = text.align_center)
        line  iSOS4Line = line.new(i_sos_watch_ll_loc, i_sos_watch_ll, bar_index, i_sos_watch_ll, color = showInternal ? color.new(iBearColor, 15) : color(na), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
        array.push(intHistLabels, iSOS4Lbl)
        array.push(intHistLines, iSOS4Line)
        if not na(i_sw_line)
            line.set_x2(i_sw_line, bar_index)
            i_sw_line := na
            
        i_sos_watch_hh     := i_sw_price
        i_sos_watch_hh_loc := i_sw_loc
        
        int_bear_break := true
        int_bear_sos   := true
        int_break_origin_loc := i_sw_loc

        i_sw_lbl          := na
        i_sw_price        := na
        i_tracked_ext     := na
        i_tracked_ext_loc := na
        i_last_hl         := na
        i_pb_count        := 0
        i_pb_started      := false
        i_pb_lqc          := na
        i_pb_lqh          := na
        i_last_mode       := -1
        i_mode            := -1
        i_sos_watch_ll    := na

// ── Update last_mode when mode changes ───────────────────
if internalActive and i_mode != 0
    i_last_mode := i_mode

// ── Extend active swing line every bar ────────────────────
if internalActive and not na(i_sw_line)
    line.set_x2(i_sw_line, bar_index)

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  CANDLESTICKS — ported from repo32, self-contained, location-agnostic
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Runs on whatever timeframe it is called from. It knows nothing about sweeps, fibs
// or gaps and must not learn: this block is meant to be lifted into the A+ file
// unchanged and handed a different location.
//
// Returns a CODE rather than a name so the tuple crossing request.security stays
// numeric. Precedence runs strongest-first, and it decides the STOP as well as the
// label — a two-candle pattern is measured across both candles, a three-candle Star
// across all three, and a single-candle wick or Doji across its own range only.
// Taking `max(high, high[1])` for a one-candle pattern would put the stop on an
// unrelated neighbour, which is a wider stop bought for nothing.
//
//   11 Sweep + Engulf (ranked first — strictly the strongest)
//   1 Harami · 2 Engulfing · 3 Wick rejection · 4 Doji · 5 Kicker
//   6 Star   · 7 Hanging Man · 8 Shooting Star · 9 Piercing · 10 Belt
// `lag` is how far back the answer is read. 1 = the last CLOSED bar, which is the
// non-repainting read for a HIGHER timeframe. 0 = this bar, which is correct and safe only
// when the caller is on the same timeframe. `simple int` is required — Pine will not accept
// a series value as a history offset.
f_candles(simple int lag) =>
    float lower10 = ta.lowest(low, 10)[1]
    float body    = math.abs(open - close)
    float rng     = high - low

    bool cDoji        = body <= rng * dojiSize
    // ── The one pattern here that is NOT repo32's ────────────────────────────
    // Took out the previous candle's extreme and closed clean through the other side.
    // It is a SWEEP measured against the previous candle, nested inside the H4 sweep the
    // setup already required — two grabs at one location, not a duplicate of one.
    // Deliberately says nothing about the previous candle's colour or body, unlike the
    // Engulfing below: what matters is that its wick was taken and its whole range lost.
    bool cBearSwpEng  = high > high[1] and close < low[1]
    bool cBullSwpEng  = low  < low[1]  and close > high[1]
    // ⚠ Each of the rest is repo32's line with its trailing `open[trend]` term removed
    // and NOTHING else touched. See THE TREND FILTER IS GONE in the header.
    bool cBearHarami  = close[1] > open[1] and open > close and open <= close[1] and open[1] <= close and open - close < close[1] - open[1]
    bool cBullHarami  = open[1] > close[1] and close > open and close <= open[1] and close[1] <= open and close - open < open[1] - close[1]
    bool cBearEng     = close[1] > open[1] and open > close and open >= close[1] and open[1] >= close and open - close > close[1] - open[1]
    bool cBullEng     = open[1] > close[1] and close > open and close >= open[1] and close[1] >= open and close - open > open[1] - close[1]
    bool cPiercing    = close[1] < open[1] and open < low[1] and close > close[1] + ((open[1] - close[1]) / 2) and close < open[1]
    bool cBullBelt    = low == open and open < lower10 and open < close and close > ((high[1] - low[1]) / 2) + low[1]
    bool cBullKick    = open[1] > close[1] and open >= open[1] and close > open
    bool cBearKick    = open[1] < close[1] and open <= open[1] and close <= open
    bool cHangingMan  = (rng > 4 * body) and ((close - low) / (0.001 + rng) >= 0.75) and ((open - low) / (0.001 + rng) >= 0.75) and high[1] < open and high[2] < open
    bool cEveningStar = close[2] > open[2] and math.min(open[1], close[1]) > close[2] and open < math.min(open[1], close[1]) and close < open
    bool cMorningStar = close[2] < open[2] and math.max(open[1], close[1]) < close[2] and open > math.max(open[1], close[1]) and close > open
    bool cShootStar   = open[1] < close[1] and open > close[1] and high - math.max(open, close) >= body * 3 and math.min(close, open) - low <= body
    bool cHammer      = (rng > 3 * body) and ((close - low) / (0.001 + rng) > 0.6) and ((open - low) / (0.001 + rng) > 0.6)
    bool cInvHammer   = (rng > 3 * body) and ((high - close) / (0.001 + rng) > 0.6) and ((high - open) / (0.001 + rng) > 0.6)

    int bCode = patBearSwpEng and cBearSwpEng ? 11 : patBearEng and cBearEng ? 2 : patBearHarami and cBearHarami ? 1 : patEveningStar and cEveningStar ? 6 : patBearKick and cBearKick ? 5 : patHangingMan and cHangingMan ? 7 : patShootStar and cShootStar ? 8 : patInvHammer and cInvHammer ? 3 : patBearDoji and cDoji ? 4 : 0
    int sCode = patBullSwpEng and cBullSwpEng ? 11 : patBullEng and cBullEng ? 2 : patBullHarami and cBullHarami ? 1 : patMornStar and cMorningStar ? 6 : patBullKick and cBullKick ? 5 : patPiercing and cPiercing ? 9 : patBullBelt and cBullBelt ? 10 : patHammer and cHammer ? 3 : patBullDoji and cDoji ? 4 : 0

    int bN = bCode == 6 ? 3 : (bCode == 1 or bCode == 2 or bCode == 5 or bCode == 11) ? 2 : 1
    int sN = sCode == 6 ? 3 : (sCode == 1 or sCode == 2 or sCode == 5 or sCode == 9 or sCode == 11) ? 2 : 1

    // The candle BEFORE the pattern candle, as a direction. Numeric so the tuple stays
    // numeric across request.security. 1 = up · -1 = down · 0 = flat.
    int cPrev = close[1] > open[1] ? 1 : close[1] < open[1] ? -1 : 0

    // BOTH extremes of each pattern's span. The high is the stop for a short and the low
    // is the stop for a long, so the Invert switch needs the other one — without it an
    // inverted trade would have to stop at a price on the wrong side of its own entry.
    float bHi = bN == 3 ? math.max(math.max(high, high[1]), high[2]) : bN == 2 ? math.max(high, high[1]) : high
    float bLo = bN == 3 ? math.min(math.min(low,  low[1]),  low[2])  : bN == 2 ? math.min(low,  low[1])  : low
    float sLo = sN == 3 ? math.min(math.min(low,  low[1]),  low[2])  : sN == 2 ? math.min(low,  low[1])  : low
    float sHi = sN == 3 ? math.max(math.max(high, high[1]), high[2]) : sN == 2 ? math.max(high, high[1]) : high

    // Everything is returned one bar back. Combined with lookahead_on at the call
    // site this is Pine's canonical non-repainting higher-timeframe read: it hands
    // over the LAST CLOSED confirmation bar, identical on history and in realtime.
    // Without it the forming 15m bar's pattern flickers true and false intrabar and a
    // latch would catch a candle that never existed.
    // ATR rides out on this tuple rather than being taken on the chart, because it stands
    // in for the SIZE OF THE 15m PATTERN. A 5m ATR would be roughly a third of the right
    // scale and would produce stops far tighter than the candle they replace — which is
    // the collapsing-stop hazard, not a tighter risk.
    [bCode[lag], bHi[lag], bLo[lag], sCode[lag], sLo[lag], sHi[lag], close[lag], time_close[lag], ta.atr(atrLen)[lag], cPrev[lag]]

f_patName(int c, bool isBear) =>
    switch c
        1  => "Harami"
        2  => "Engulfing"
        3  => isBear ? "Inv Hammer" : "Hammer"
        4  => "Doji"
        5  => "Kicker"
        6  => isBear ? "Evening Star" : "Morning Star"
        7  => "Hanging Man"
        8  => "Shooting Star"
        9  => "Piercing"
        10 => "Belt"
        11 => "Sweep+Engulf"
        => ""

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  HIGHER-TIMEFRAME READS
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// The LEVELS come up from the liquidity timeframe, but the SWEEP is detected on the
// chart's own bars — so a level taken at 15:07 is known at 15:07, not at the H4
// close. Same split mpc_assistant.pine uses for its H4 tracker.
[liqTime, liqPrevHi, liqPrevLo] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tfLiq, [time, high[1], low[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
bool newLiqBar = ta.change(liqTime) != 0

// TWO reads, and the pairing of lag with lookahead is what makes both of them honest.
// Delayed  = lag 1 + lookahead ON  — Pine's canonical non-repainting higher-timeframe read.
// Live     = lag 0 + lookahead OFF — this bar's own value, never a peek at a forming one.
// Pairing them the other way round is the classic repaint bug: lag 0 with lookahead ON
// hands history a bar that had not finished, and the backtest prints results nobody could
// have traded. Both are computed and one is selected, because `lookahead` must be a
// constant and so cannot be switched by an input.
[dBearCode, dBearHi, dBearLo, dBullCode, dBullLo, dBullHi, dClose, dTime, dAtr, dPrevDir] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tfConf, f_candles(1), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[lBearCode, lBearHi, lBearLo, lBullCode, lBullLo, lBullHi, lClose, lTime, lAtr, lPrevDir] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tfConf, f_candles(0), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)

int   cBearCode = confLive ? lBearCode : dBearCode
float cBearHi   = confLive ? lBearHi   : dBearHi
float cBearLo   = confLive ? lBearLo   : dBearLo
int   cBullCode = confLive ? lBullCode : dBullCode
float cBullLo   = confLive ? lBullLo   : dBullLo
float cBullHi   = confLive ? lBullHi   : dBullHi
float cClose    = confLive ? lClose    : dClose
int   cTime     = confLive ? lTime     : dTime
float cAtr      = confLive ? lAtr      : dAtr
int   cPrevDir  = confLive ? lPrevDir  : dPrevDir

bool newConfBar = cTime != cTime[1]

// The previous-candle filter, resolved per side. For a SELL the level is above, so
// "ran into the level" means that candle was rising (cPrevDir == 1); the BUY case mirrors.
bool prevOkBear = prevDir == "Any" or (prevDir == "Ran into the level" ? cPrevDir ==  1 : cPrevDir == -1)
bool prevOkBull = prevDir == "Any" or (prevDir == "Ran into the level" ? cPrevDir == -1 : cPrevDir ==  1)

float emaVal = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, emaTf, ta.ema(close, emaLen)[1], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  SETUP STATE — one window, one setup
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Everything here is scoped to a single liquidity candle and wiped when the next one
// opens. An OPEN TRADE is deliberately NOT wiped (Aaron, 2026-08-05): the window
// bounds the SETUP, not the position. Once the entry has triggered only the stop or
// the target closes it, and a new H4 arriving mid-trade simply starts a fresh setup
// that the one-position rule will refuse while the old trade is alive.
var float lvlHi       = na
var float lvlLo       = na
var int   setupDir    = 0     // 0 none · -1 short (high taken) · +1 long (low taken)
var int   sweepT      = na    // close time of the chart bar that took the level
var float ccLine      = na    // the confirmation candle's close — the trigger line
var float ccStop      = na    // the confirmation pattern's extreme — the stop anchor
var int   ccCode      = 0
var bool  firedWindow = false
// The direction the ORDER goes, which is the pattern's side unless Invert is on.
// `setupDir` stays the PATTERN side throughout — it is what the levels, the labels and
// the pattern names are keyed to, and flipping it would make the chart describe a candle
// that never fired.
var int   ccTradeDir  = 0
// True only on the bar a pattern armed. `entryAtConf` triggers off this, so "enter on the
// confirmation" cannot leak into later bars and enter at a price the pattern never saw.
bool armedNow = false

var line  lnHi = na, var line lnLo = na, var line lnCC = na

// ⚠ The state wipe is gated on `reqSweep`. Without that gate a new H4 candle would still
// arrive every four hours and destroy a setup the free-running path had just armed, which
// would look like patterns being ignored at random.
if newLiqBar and not na(liqPrevHi) and not na(liqPrevLo)
    lvlHi := liqPrevHi
    lvlLo := liqPrevLo
    if reqSweep
        setupDir    := 0
        ccTradeDir  := 0
        sweepT      := na
        ccLine      := na
        ccStop      := na
        ccCode      := 0
        firedWindow := false
        if not na(lnCC)
            lnCC := na
    // Not drawn when nothing reads them — a level on the chart that decides no trade is
    // the same class of lie as a label describing code that does not run.
    if showLevels and reqSweep
        lnHi := line.new(bar_index, lvlHi, bar_index + 1, lvlHi, color = LIQ_ACTIVE, width = 1)
        lnLo := line.new(bar_index, lvlLo, bar_index + 1, lvlLo, color = LIQ_ACTIVE, width = 1)

// ── THE SWEEP ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// A WICK takes the level, not a close. A sweep is price reaching the stops resting
// beyond a high; whether the candle closed back inside describes what happened AFTER
// the liquidity was taken, not whether it was taken. Same reading mpc_assistant.pine
// applies to its EQH/EQL levels and its order blocks.
// ⚠ FIRST SWEEP OWNS THE WINDOW. If the high goes and later the low goes too, the
// window is still the short setup — "for every new H4 there is A setup", singular.
// Both on one bar is unresolvable at chart resolution, so the high wins by order.
if reqSweep and setupDir == 0 and not na(lvlHi) and not na(lvlLo)
    if high > lvlHi
        setupDir := -1
        sweepT   := time_close
    else if low < lvlLo
        setupDir := 1
        sweepT   := time_close

// ── THE CONFIRMATION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The FIRST qualifying pattern to close after the sweep wins, and nothing later moves
// the line (Aaron, 2026-08-05). A line that re-anchored on every new pattern would
// walk down with price and either never trigger or trigger progressively worse.
// ⚠ `cTime > sweepT` is what enforces the ORDER, and it is a genuine test rather than
// a formality: the pattern is read on the confirmation timeframe while the sweep is
// detected on the chart, so without it a 15m candle that closed BEFORE the sweep
// could arm a setup the sweep had not yet created.
if reqSweep and setupDir != 0 and na(ccLine) and newConfBar and not na(sweepT) and cTime > sweepT
    if setupDir == -1 and cBearCode != 0 and prevOkBear
        ccLine := cClose
        ccStop := invertTrade ? cBearLo : cBearHi
        ccCode := cBearCode
        ccTradeDir := invertTrade ? 1 : -1
    else if setupDir == 1 and cBullCode != 0 and prevOkBull
        ccLine := cClose
        ccStop := invertTrade ? cBullHi : cBullLo
        ccCode := cBullCode
        ccTradeDir := invertTrade ? -1 : 1
    armedNow := not na(ccLine)

// ── THE SAME STEP WITH NO SWEEP REQUIRED ────────────────────────────────────
// The control path. Every confirmation bar is a fresh setup: the pattern supplies the
// direction, there is no window, and nothing carries over. `firedWindow` is cleared each
// time because it exists to enforce ONE setup per H4 window, and there are no windows here.
// ⚠ The new arm is built into LOCALS and only committed if a pattern actually fired.
// Writing the state first and filling it in second would mean a confirmation bar with no
// pattern — the common case — silently deleted a setup that was still waiting for its
// trigger, and the setup would live about three chart bars instead of until it is replaced.
if not reqSweep and newConfBar
    int   nDir  = 0
    float nLine = na
    float nStop = na
    int   nCode = 0
    if cBearCode != 0 and prevOkBear
        nDir  := -1
        nLine := cClose
        nStop := invertTrade ? cBearLo : cBearHi
        nCode := cBearCode
    else if cBullCode != 0 and prevOkBull
        nDir  := 1
        nLine := cClose
        nStop := invertTrade ? cBullHi : cBullLo
        nCode := cBullCode
    if nDir != 0
        setupDir    := nDir
        ccLine      := nLine
        ccStop      := nStop
        ccCode      := nCode
        ccTradeDir  := invertTrade ? -nDir : nDir
        firedWindow := false
        armedNow    := true

// Drawn from ONE place so both paths above annotate identically. The label names the
// pattern's own side; the tooltip names the TRADE, which differ when Invert is on.
if armedNow
    if showCC
        lnCC := line.new(bar_index, ccLine, bar_index + 1, ccLine, color = TRIG_ORANGE, style = line.style_solid, width = 1)
    if showConfLabel
        label.new(bar_index, ccStop, f_patName(ccCode, setupDir == -1), style = setupDir == -1 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, color = TRIG_ORANGEL, textcolor = POS_TEXT, size = size.small, tooltip = (ccTradeDir < 0 ? "SELL · " : "BUY · ") + f_patName(ccCode, setupDir == -1) + (invertTrade ? " (inverted)" : "") + "\nTrigger line " + str.tostring(ccLine, format.mintick) + "\nStop anchor " + str.tostring(ccStop, format.mintick))

// Extend whatever is live to the right edge.
if showLevels and reqSweep and not na(lnHi)
    line.set_x2(lnHi, bar_index + 1)
    line.set_x2(lnLo, bar_index + 1)
    line.set_color(lnHi, setupDir == -1 ? LIQ_SWEPT : LIQ_ACTIVE)
    line.set_color(lnLo, setupDir ==  1 ? LIQ_SWEPT : LIQ_ACTIVE)
if showCC and not na(lnCC)
    line.set_x2(lnCC, bar_index + 1)

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  ENTRY
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ONE AT A TIME (Aaron, 2026-08-05). `strategy.position_size == 0` is the whole rule:
// a setup that fires while a trade is running is skipped, never stacked. Stacking is
// the only variant where the risk per trade stops being what the input says it is.
float bufP = stopBufTk * syminfo.mintick

// f_ratchet — the runner's trail, ported from `f_swingRatchet` in mpc_strategy.pine with
// the one change this file forces: A+ anchors on the last confirmed swing, and there is no
// structure engine here, so the anchor is the breakeven stop. From that anchor the stop
// climbs one `pct`-of-price step for every step of favourable move.
// It returns the ANCHOR until the move is one full step past it, so the trail can never be
// looser than breakeven — only equal or tighter. That is what makes it safe to call from
// the moment TP1 is touched.
f_ratchet(float anchor, float maxFav, int dir, float pct) =>
    float step = maxFav * pct / 100.0
    float run  = (maxFav - anchor) * dir
    float out  = anchor
    if step > 0 and not na(run) and run >= step
        float steps = math.floor((run - step) / step)
        out := anchor + steps * step * dir
    out

// ⚠ Keyed to ccTradeDir, NOT setupDir — with Invert on they are opposites, and the trigger
// has to follow the ORDER. The line test flips with it: a trade that is short wants a close
// below the line whichever pattern armed it.
bool canEnter  = ccTradeDir != 0 and not na(ccLine) and not na(ccStop) and not firedWindow and strategy.position_size == 0
bool trigShort = canEnter and ccTradeDir == -1 and (entryAtConf ? armedNow : close < ccLine)
bool trigLong  = canEnter and ccTradeDir ==  1 and (entryAtConf ? armedNow : close > ccLine)

// ⚠ Judged on the TRADE, not on the candle. A short needs price below the EMA.
bool emaOkShort = not useEma or (not na(emaVal) and close < emaVal)
bool emaOkLong  = not useEma or (not na(emaVal) and close > emaVal)

var float tEntry = na, var float tStop = na, var float tTp1 = na
var int   tDir = 0, var int tBar = na, var string tPat = ""
var float tRiskUsd = na, var float tNetAtEntry = na
// `tStop` is the trade's FROZEN opening stop and is never rewritten — it is the 1R
// yardstick every R number here is measured against, and the price the log reports.
// The LIVE stop is `curStop` below, recomputed each bar from the stage.
var int   tStage  = 0   // 0 = opening stop · 1 = TP1 touched → breakeven, then the ratchet
var float tMaxFav = na  // high-water mark of the open trade, drives the ratchet

// ⚠ THE TRIGGER IS ONE SHOT, WHETHER OR NOT IT BECOMES A TRADE. `firedWindow` is set
// on the trigger itself, not on the order — so a close beyond the line that a filter
// REFUSES kills the setup rather than leaving it armed to retry on the next bar. The
// rule is "the FIRST close beyond the line"; a retry would enter deeper on a later
// candle and quietly stop being that rule.
bool tookShort = false
bool tookLong  = false

// ── PARITY RECORD — WRITE-ONLY ───────────────────────────────────────────────
// NOTHING in this file reads these four. They exist so `mpc_h4_sweep_strategy_export.pine`
// can COPY the refusal this gate made, rather than re-deriving it from prices further down
// the file. `okMin` / `okTrig` / `emaOk*` are locals inside the two trigger blocks and are
// gone by the time anything else runs, so without this the export would have to recompute
// them — a SECOND implementation of the gate, which is exactly what every other export twin
// in this repo is built to avoid. A copied value cannot disagree with the thing it copied.
//
// hTrigCode: 0 = the trigger was TAKEN · 1 = stop distance not positive (an `na` ATR, or a
// pattern extreme on the wrong side of the close) · 2 = stop too tight for `minStopPct` ·
// 3 = the trigger candle closed too far past the line for `maxTrigPct` · 4 = the EMA filter.
// ⚠ 5 = the trade DIRECTION is switched off. Numbered last and ranked FIRST: a code is a WIRE
// FORMAT that px_blk carries into an export already on disk, so an existing number can never be
// renumbered — only its place in the chain moves, and a disabled side refuses before anything else.
// Ordered as the `if` reads them, so the code names the FIRST rule that refused rather than
// whichever one happens to be checked last.
var int   hTrigCode = 0
var int   hTrigBar  = na
var float hTrigPx   = na   // the entry price the trigger would have taken — set on a refusal too
var float hTrigStop = na   // the stop it would have carried
// ⚠ THE SIDE HAS TO BE RECORDED RATHER THAN INFERRED, and `mpc_d_strategy.pine` already paid for
// learning that. Its blocked tag read the direction off the SOS that fired on the same bar, which
// was correct only while every candidate arrived on one — and the moment a second entry mode
// existed, every candidate drew as a SHORT. Here the equivalent shortcut would be reading
// `trigShort`, which is a per-bar local: correct today, and silent the day a refusal is reported
// from anywhere but these two blocks.
var int   hTrigDir  = 0    // +1 long / -1 short, for EVERY trigger, taken or refused

if trigShort
    // ⚠ A DISABLED SIDE DOES NOT CONSUME THE WINDOW, unlike every other refusal here. A
    // stop-too-tight refusal is about this setup; 'shorts off' is about every short in the run,
    // and burning the window would silently remove LONGS that shared it — so a long-only
    // measurement would not be the long book.
    if execShorts
        firedWindow := true
    // ATR mode with no ATR yet leaves `sp` na, so `risk` is na and `risk > 0` is false —
    // the setup is refused rather than entered on a stop nobody could compute.
    float sp   = slMode == "ATR" ? close + cAtr * slMult : ccStop + bufP
    float risk = sp - close
    bool  okMin  = minStopPct <= 0 or risk >= close * minStopPct / 100.0
    bool  okTrig = maxTrigPct <= 0 or (ccLine - close) <= risk * maxTrigPct / 100.0
    hTrigBar  := bar_index
    hTrigPx   := close
    hTrigStop := sp
    hTrigDir  := -1
    hTrigCode := not execShorts ? 5 : na(risk) or risk <= 0 ? 1 : not okMin ? 2 : not okTrig ? 3 : not emaOkShort ? 4 : 0
    if execShorts and risk > 0 and okMin and okTrig and emaOkShort
        tEntry := close
        tStop  := sp
        tTp1   := close - risk * tp1R
        tDir   := -1
        tBar   := bar_index
        tStage := 0
        tMaxFav := close
        tPat   := f_patName(ccCode, true)
        // R is measured off the size ACTUALLY sent, not off the size we wanted, so the R
        // labels stay honest under fixed sizing instead of quietly describing a different
        // position from the one the tester opened.
        float q = sizeMode == "Fixed contracts" ? fixedQty : (strategy.equity * riskPct / 100.0) / risk
        tRiskUsd    := risk * q
        tNetAtEntry := strategy.netprofit
        tookShort := true
        strategy.entry("Short", strategy.short, qty = q, comment = tPat)

if trigLong
    if execLongs
        firedWindow := true
    float sp   = slMode == "ATR" ? close - cAtr * slMult : ccStop - bufP
    float risk = close - sp
    bool  okMin  = minStopPct <= 0 or risk >= close * minStopPct / 100.0
    bool  okTrig = maxTrigPct <= 0 or (close - ccLine) <= risk * maxTrigPct / 100.0
    hTrigBar  := bar_index
    hTrigPx   := close
    hTrigStop := sp
    hTrigDir  := 1
    hTrigCode := not execLongs ? 5 : na(risk) or risk <= 0 ? 1 : not okMin ? 2 : not okTrig ? 3 : not emaOkLong ? 4 : 0
    if execLongs and risk > 0 and okMin and okTrig and emaOkLong
        tEntry := close
        tStop  := sp
        tTp1   := close + risk * tp1R
        tDir   := 1
        tBar   := bar_index
        tStage := 0
        tMaxFav := close
        tPat   := f_patName(ccCode, false)
        float q = sizeMode == "Fixed contracts" ? fixedQty : (strategy.equity * riskPct / 100.0) / risk
        tRiskUsd    := risk * q
        tNetAtEntry := strategy.netprofit
        tookLong := true
        strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long, qty = q, comment = tPat)

// ══ BLOCKED-SETUP TAG ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// A confirmation candle fired inside a live sweep window — the one structural fact this
// strategy is built on — and a gate refused it. These are the only setups that are invisible
// everywhere else: no order is sent, so nothing is drawn, no row reaches the trade list, and
// the Strategy Tester cannot know they existed. That makes it impossible to judge whether a
// gate is protecting the account or costing it. Now each one prints a PINK tag with the reason
// on hover and a dotted leader to the price the entry would have taken — so you can flip the
// gate off, re-run, and compare.
//
// ⚠ IT READS `hTrigCode`, WHICH THE TRIGGER BLOCKS ALREADY WROTE, and does not re-derive
// anything. `okMin` / `okTrig` / `emaOk*` are locals inside those blocks, so recomputing the
// refusal here would be a SECOND implementation of the gate that can disagree with the gate —
// the trap the export twin's own header records. The tag and the export's px_blk therefore
// cannot tell different stories, because they read one variable.
//
// ⚠ NO DEDUPE, unlike A+'s marker, and it is not an omission: a trigger fires at most ONCE per
// H4 window (`firedWindow`), so one refusal is already one bar. A+ needs its sosBar+code key
// because a setup there can stay refused for twenty consecutive bars.
//
// ⚠ `hTrigBar == bar_index` is what scopes it to THIS bar. The four `hTrig*` fields are `var`
// and keep the last trigger's values for ever, so without that test the tag would redraw the
// same refusal on every bar until the next trigger replaced it.
f_hBlkWhy(int c) =>
    switch c
        1 => "Stop distance is not positive — either the ATR is not warm yet, or the pattern's own extreme sits on the wrong side of the close. Nothing can be sized against it."
        2 => "Minimum stop distance — the stop sits closer to the entry than your floor, so this position would be oversized and noise-sensitive."
        3 => "Trigger too far past the line — the confirmation candle closed further beyond the confirmation-close line than 'maxTrigPct' allows, so the entry is chasing rather than fading."
        4 => "Trend EMA filter — the confirmation candle is on the wrong side of the EMA for this direction."
        5 => "'Trade longs' / 'Trade shorts' is OFF for this side. ⚠ Unlike every other refusal here, this one does NOT consume the H4 window — so the other side's book is exactly what it would have been."
        => ""

if showBlockTag and hTrigBar == bar_index and hTrigCode != 0 and hTrigDir != 0 and not na(hTrigPx) and not na(cAtr)
    bool  bLong = hTrigDir == 1
    float tagY  = bLong ? low - cAtr * 2 : high + cAtr * 2
    line.new(bar_index, hTrigPx, bar_index, tagY, color = BLK_PINKL, style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
    label.new(bar_index, tagY, (bLong ? "▲" : "▼") + " SETUP BLOCKED", tooltip = (bLong ? "▲ LONG" : "▼ SHORT") + " blocked\n──────────────────\n" + f_hBlkWhy(hTrigCode) + "\n──────────────────\nEntry would have been " + str.tostring(hTrigPx, format.mintick) + "\nStop would have been " + str.tostring(hTrigStop, format.mintick), color = BLK_PINK, textcolor = POS_TEXT, style = bLong ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, size = size.small)

// ── Stage the stop ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ⚠ `bar_index > tBar` EXCLUDES THE ENTRY BAR, and it is load-bearing. The entry fills at
// this bar's CLOSE (process_orders_on_close), so everything the candle did before that
// close happened while the trade did not exist — reading its extreme as favourable
// movement is how `BUG_exit_fill_price_mismatch.md` promoted a stop to breakeven on a move
// the position was never in, which then sits on the wrong side of the market and blows the
// trade out at the next bar's open. A+ guards this with `position_size[1]`; that test is
// wrong here, because with fills on the close `position_size` is still 0 when the script
// runs on the entry bar, so `[1]` would also skip the first REAL bar of the trade.
// Every later bar counts: the trade held through all of it.
if strategy.position_size != 0 and bar_index > tBar and not na(tMaxFav)
    tMaxFav := tDir > 0 ? math.max(tMaxFav, high) : math.min(tMaxFav, low)
    if tStage < 1 and (tDir > 0 ? high >= tTp1 : low <= tTp1)
        tStage := 1

// Stage 1 is tied to the TP1 TOUCH, not to an R distance. TP1 is a limit order, so keying
// breakeven off the touch is what guarantees the partial banks BEFORE the rest of the
// position is protected — an R trigger can fire on a wick that never filled the limit and
// then protects a trade that has taken no profit at all.
float beStop  = na(tEntry) ? na : tEntry + tDir * beBufTk * syminfo.mintick
float ratchet = tStage >= 1 and not na(beStop) ? f_ratchet(beStop, tMaxFav, tDir, trailPct) : na
float curStop = tStage >= 1 ? (na(ratchet) ? beStop : ratchet) : tStop

// The brackets are re-issued every bar so the stop can move. Two details, both of which
// leave a real hole if they are "tidied":
//
// ⚠ `or tookLong` PLACES THE BRACKET ON THE ENTRY BAR, and without it the trade spends its
// first bar with no stop. `process_orders_on_close` fills the entry at THIS bar's close, so
// `strategy.position_size` is still 0 while the script runs here — a position-size test
// alone would not place an exit until the next bar's close, and anything the market did in
// between would have gone unguarded. Pine accepts an exit for an entry order that has not
// filled yet, so issuing both on the same bar is the correct shape.
//
// ⚠ TP1 STOPS BEING RE-ISSUED ONCE TOUCHED. `strategy.exit` with an id whose order already
// FILLED places a NEW order rather than modifying the old one, so a re-issued rung would
// bank another slice of the runner every bar, at a limit the market is already past. The
// A+ file re-issues its rungs unconditionally and gets away with it only because its rungs
// ship at 0% and the call is skipped entirely — do not copy that shape here.
if strategy.position_size > 0 or tookLong
    if tp1Pct > 0 and tStage < 1
        strategy.exit("L-TP1", from_entry = "Long", qty_percent = tp1Pct, limit = tTp1, stop = curStop)
    strategy.exit("L-RUN", from_entry = "Long", stop = curStop)
if strategy.position_size < 0 or tookShort
    if tp1Pct > 0 and tStage < 1
        strategy.exit("S-TP1", from_entry = "Short", qty_percent = tp1Pct, limit = tTp1, stop = curStop)
    strategy.exit("S-RUN", from_entry = "Short", stop = curStop)

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  DRAWING THE TRADE
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Red from entry to the opening stop, green from entry to TP1 — the picture from Aaron's
// own position tool. Both boxes are frozen at the PLAN, so they still describe what was
// risked and where the half came off even after the stop has moved.
// ⚠ THERE IS NO BOX FOR THE RUNNER, and that is the honest drawing rather than a missing
// one: TP2 is a trail, so the runner has no target price to draw a box to. What it has is
// a stop that moves, and that is the dashed line — watch it leave the entry and climb.
var box bxRisk = na, var box bxTp1 = na

if (tookShort or tookLong) and showTrade and not na(tEntry)
    bxRisk := box.new(bar_index, math.max(tEntry, tStop), bar_index + 1, math.min(tEntry, tStop), bgcolor = POS_DD, border_color = color(na))
    bxTp1  := box.new(bar_index, math.max(tEntry, tTp1),  bar_index + 1, math.min(tEntry, tTp1),  bgcolor = POS_G1, border_color = color(na))

if strategy.position_size != 0 and not na(bxRisk)
    box.set_right(bxRisk, bar_index + 1)
    box.set_right(bxTp1,  bar_index + 1)

// The moving stop, one segment per staged bar — the staircase IS the trail, and watching
// it is the only way to judge whether the ratchet step is too loose. Drawn only while
// staged, so it costs nothing on the trades that never reach TP1.
// ⚠ Segments past `max_lines_count` are dropped oldest-first by TradingView, so on a long
// backtest the early trades lose their staircase. The trade boxes are unaffected.
if showTrade and strategy.position_size != 0 and tStage >= 1 and not na(curStop) and not na(curStop[1])
    line.new(bar_index - 1, curStop[1], bar_index, curStop, color = POS_STOPLN, style = line.style_dashed, width = 1)

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  RESULT
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Graded in R against the dollars actually put at risk, so a win and a loss are
// comparable across a $2 stop and a $20 one. That is the entire reason the sizing is
// percent-of-equity rather than a fixed lot.
float closedR = strategy.position_size == 0 and strategy.position_size[1] != 0 and not na(tRiskUsd) and tRiskUsd > 0 ? (strategy.netprofit - tNetAtEntry) / tRiskUsd : na

if not na(closedR)
    if showTrade and not na(bxRisk)
        box.set_right(bxRisk, bar_index)
        box.set_right(bxTp1,  bar_index)
    if showConfLabel
        label.new(bar_index, close, (closedR >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(closedR, "#.##") + "R", style = tDir < 0 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = math.abs(closedR) <= H4_BE_BAND ? POS_BE : closedR > 0 ? POS_WIN : POS_LOSS, textcolor = POS_TEXT, size = size.small, tooltip = tPat + "\nEntry " + str.tostring(tEntry, format.mintick) + "\nStop  " + str.tostring(tStop, format.mintick) + "\nTP1   " + str.tostring(tTp1, format.mintick) + (tStage >= 1 ? " · HIT, runner trailed" : " · never reached"))

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  LOG
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Every line carries the PATTERN. Harami and Engulfing are exact complements on a
// continuous instrument, so one tagged run answers "which pattern is carrying this"
// by slicing — no second and third run needed.
if logTrades and (tookShort or tookLong) and not na(tEntry)
    log.info("[ENTRY @" + str.tostring(bar_index) + "] " + (tDir < 0 ? "SHORT" : "LONG") + " · " + tPat +
      " · entry " + str.tostring(tEntry, format.mintick) +
      " · stop " + str.tostring(tStop, format.mintick) +
      " · tp1 " + str.tostring(tTp1, format.mintick) + " @" + str.tostring(tp1Pct, "#") + "%" +
      " · risk " + str.tostring(math.abs(tEntry - tStop), format.mintick) +
      " · line " + str.tostring(ccLine, format.mintick) +
      (reqSweep ? " · level " + str.tostring(setupDir < 0 ? lvlHi : lvlLo, format.mintick) : " · no sweep required") +
      (invertTrade ? " · INVERTED" : ""))

if logTrades and not na(closedR)
    log.info("[RESULT] " + (tDir < 0 ? "SHORT" : "LONG") + " · " + tPat + " · " +
      (math.abs(closedR) < 0.05 ? "SCRATCH" : closedR > 0 ? "WIN" : "LOSS") + " " +
      (closedR >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(closedR, "#.##") + "R · " +
      (tStage >= 1 ? "TP1 hit, ran to " + str.tostring(math.abs(tMaxFav - tEntry) / math.abs(tEntry - tStop), "#.##") + "R" : "stopped before TP1") + " · " +
      str.tostring(bar_index - tBar) + " bars · equity $" + str.tostring(strategy.equity, "#.##"))

// Entry markers, so a trade is never invisible even when the boxes are switched off.
// Keyed off tookShort/tookLong, NOT off strategy.position_size: with
// process_orders_on_close the fill lands at this bar's close, AFTER the script has
// run, so position_size is still 0 here and a size test would draw the marker one
// bar late — or, on a trade that opens and closes quickly, not at all.
plotshape(tookShort, title = "Short entry", style = shape.triangledown, location = location.abovebar, color = POS_REDB, size = size.small)
plotshape(tookLong,  title = "Long entry",  style = shape.triangleup,   location = location.belowbar, color = POS_GREENB, size = size.small)

// The EMA, drawn only when it is actually filtering. A line on the chart that nothing
// reads is the same class of lie as a label describing code that does not run.
plot(useEma ? emaVal : na, title = "Trend EMA", color = POS_OPENL, linewidth = 2)
